{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded","id":1052247,"title":"Ysyr and the Dragon Blooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-20T16:07:14-08:00","id":1052247,"title":"Ysyr and the Dragon Blooded","content":"So... A player of mine is playing a Ysyrian sorceress that Exalted as a Twilight, and we were going over her backstory. She suggested to me that she actually doesn't have an inherent problem with the Solar Exalted, and figured that her view of them was that they were ancient powerful and enlightened people, with all the risks that go along with that sort of thing... but no view of them as Anathema or evil.<br /> <br /> She reasoned that that Ys probably have no use for the Immaculates, and that most of the sorcerers in Ysyr are probably mortals.<br /> <br /> It occurred to me: She might actually be right about that. I read back over the Ysyr bits in the book but there's nothing to suggest that they have a significant Dragon Blooded force on their side. Or even that they have any at all.<br /> <br /> Then the line about how you're either a sorcerer or a slave. Well... Not every Dragon Blood can be a sorcerer. I know the book technically lets anyone take that charm with the right abilities, but that's just game mechanics.<br /> <br /> So... What do y'all think? Do you think Ysyr even has any DBs to speak of? You think maybe most -- or even all -- of their DBs screw off to Prasad or somewhere else, because they want to live somewhere where they can make something of themselves?<br /> <br /> ... Do you think they <b>enslave </b>their non-sorcerous DBs? Or, hell, maybe they don't even have any at all? Maybe the blood is so thin that their exaltation rate is almost non-existant?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:54:21-08:00","id":1052275,"title":"","content":"Is it possible that there are Dragon-Blooded among the Ys? Sure.<br /> <br /> Are the ruling class composed of Dragon-Blooded? Almost certainly not.<br /> <br /> Would I call the thaumatocrat rulers of Ysyr, who apparently are capable of enslaving the raksha mortals? I wouldn't. The ruling class are sorcerers for one, and for two, I'm sure they've done things to themselves or found things that might place them somewhere adjacent to mortals.<br /> <br /> Are the people of Ysyr Immaculates? Probably not. I really doubt it. What does their religion or culture look like? Not sure! I imagine a cool answer might be that if they 'worship' anything, it is likely themselves/their forebears. They might look at Solar Artifice, but not look to the Solars themselves, if that makes sense. It's the difference between seeing yourself as the inheritor of Rome 's legacy and as subjects of the Eternal City, you know what I mean?<br /> <br /> How would they see Solars? That's a great question! I think it's really a matter of what you want your game to look like. If it were me, I think the rulers of Ysyr would seek to exploit the power of the Solars and be wary of them. Would they submit, to a Solar or a group of them? Probably not. They're a power in the Dreaming Sea that's been around a long time, and they likely have some fairly powerful sorcerers among them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:55:01-08:00","id":1052277,"title":"","content":"There isn't any kind of &quot;official&quot; ruling on what the exactly population of Ysyr is, whether it's run by Dragon Blooded or humans, or whatever. So just go with what you feel will make your chronicle better and more interesting. <br /> <br /> Personally, I think it might be interesting if it doesn't have a permanent population of Dragon Blooded. Mortals, sorcerers, godblooded yes. But no Dragon Blooded. The city may occasionally accept Dragon Blooded who seek to learn sorcery but it quickly makes them leave afterwards. And any mortal in the city who does Exalt as a Terrestrial is &quot;banished&quot; from the city (they'll give the Dragon Blooded and his family a modest amount of money and then send them somewhere else). They simply have no desire to bend their knee to anyone, and Terrestrial Exalted tend to live for so long and be so powerful that one of them would inevitably end up with more control over the city than anyone would feel comfortable with.<br /> <br /> You could even write some background that the city used to have a Terrestrial tyrant until he was overthrown by the Sorcerer-Kings and they have no desire to see anything like that repeat itself, so they do their best to ensure that Dragon Blooded don't stay within the city long enough to cause any potential problems. They could easily have a somewhat similar view on other Exalted (Solars, Lunars, etc) - powerful beings they don't want sticking around for too long and moving into a leadership position.<br /> <br /> Of course, you could easily change this to whatever you want depending on what kind of interacts you decide Ysyr has had with other Exalted. <br /> <br /> Maybe there's a neighboring No Moon Lunar who has quietly been helping the city out for the last several centuries, so the leaders there are more accepting of Lunars than they otherwise might be. Maybe some Solar hero died valiantly protecting the city 300 years ago, and his legend is still talked about today so everyone has a good opinion on Solars. Or maybe some Solar tried to hold a revolution a long time ago and now the Sorcerer-Kings of Ysyr teach that all Solars <i>are</i> horrible demons who should be killed whenever possible.<br /> <br /> Lots of possibilities. Really, I'd suggest working with your player to decide on whatever the two of you think would be most interesting for the campaign. There are lots of ways you could do things, and off hand your players idea sounds pretty reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T17:11:23-08:00","id":1052285,"title":"","content":"Given the expansion of the world, both literal and mechanical, and the distance between the Dreaming Sea and the Realm, I find it pretty hard to believe the Realm has really any influence there at all. It's somewhat like Rome having influence over South America. It's a vast, uncharted distance. I don't doubt that a 'silk road' type trade relationship might exist but I like to propose the Prasadi Dragonblooded are far more culturally removed than the canon does.<br /> <br /> I kinda find the notion that the Realm wishes to 'expand its power over the Dreaming Sea' also pretty silly - these are (to me) very 2e sentiments that poorly represent the vastness of the 3e take on geography and national borders. The Realm has far more localized places to draw trade goods and spices from that are far more productive uses of the treasury. I don't doubt they end up with goods from the Dreaming Sea, but these are likely provided by an informal chain of merchant transactions across dozens of cultures.<br /> <br /> I have few criticisms of the Dreaming Sea because it's pretty awesome but Prasad never quite clicked for me. I rewrote it a bit.<br /> <br /> So the Yser? I'd FULLY support them being virtually untouched by Realm authority, and possibly even removed enough to say sincerely, 'Wait, what 'Realm' are you talking about?'. I prefer a huge world with isolated cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T17:29:23-08:00","id":1052291,"title":"","content":"Something about this initial question feels very strange to me, since it seems to assume that places having a noteworthy group of Dragon Blooded is the norm.<br /> <br /> \u200bI expect outcastes in Ysyr are about the same as outcastes anywhere; highly unlikely on the provincial scale.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven if the write-up for Ysyr had not specifically attributed their sorcerers to mutation (or described the whole thing as operating on a class system), given the existence of non-Exalted sorcerers I would have defaulted to the assumption that they or any other mentioned sorcerers are not Exalted unless specifically described otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think they <b>enslave </b>their non-sorcerous DBs?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b{briefly presuming that the culture of Ysyr is more than about three hundred years old, and will check back on the book later}<br /> <br /> \u200bI think on the one occasion where somebody from Ysyr Exalted as anything about five hundred years ago, if that person didn't already want to become a sorcerer in order to integrate smoothly into the existing class structure, then the thaumatocrats elaborated some highly specific social and legal terminology to describe the one Exalt who happened there ever as belonging to some kind of category distinct from the usual caste system without actually undermining it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T17:31:36-08:00","id":1052293,"title":"","content":"See, I'm not worried about whether or not they're Immaculates. I'm sure they're not. I'm also not worried about the Realm's influence on them.<br /> <br /> I'm mostly trying to nail down in my head two major points: How the Ys feel about Dragon Bloods as a whole, and whether they see Solars/Lunars as Anathema or not.<br /> <br /> It's like, Buddhists might not recognize Lucifer/Samael/Satan/Whatever, but if they see something that looks like a demon, they probably wouldn't trust it much, yeah?<br /> <br /> But, then... We don't know a thing about Ysyr. Maybe they <b>don't</b> buy into the whole Anathema thing. Maybe they barely even acknowledge it, whether out of a sense of self-superiority, or because they've got Exalts among them, or whatever.<br /> <br /> It's a question. And I'm mostly interested in how other people interpret it, and whether anyone's really thought about it at all.<br /> <br /> Until my player put that in her backstory, I'll be honest and say I hadn't even considered it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T17:36:08-08:00","id":1052295,"title":"","content":"I think I would take heed of what the book says about spirits. Whether the Ys believe them to be Anathema or not is largely academic compared to the idea that Solars or Lunars (who I'm sure they've had at least I one or two run-ins with!) are very dangerous and very powerful, something which would leave them inclined to approach them with caution but possibly without the religious baggage which dictates that they should destroy them.<br /> <br /> I imagine a Ys who Exalte with the blood of the Dragons might become an important person, but that Prasad might leave them with a low opinion of the Dragon-Blooded as dangerous rivals to their hegemony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T17:39:40-08:00","id":1052297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052295#post1052295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I would take heed of what the book says about spirits. Whether the Ys believe them to be Anathema or not is largely academic compared to the idea that Solars or Lunars (who I'm sure they've had at least I one or two run-ins with!) are very dangerous and very powerful, something which would leave them inclined to approach them with caution but possibly without the religious baggage which dictates that they should destroy them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'mma have to disagree with the assertion that it's academic. There's a pretty significant difference between &quot;This thing is powerful and I should be very careful around it,&quot; vs &quot;This thing is a demon from Hell that is going to try to eat my soul and I should find someone to help me kill it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T18:02:12-08:00","id":1052307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052293#post1052293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the Ys feel about Dragon Bloods as a whole, and whether they see Solars/Lunars as Anathema or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt should be kept in mind that the wider cultural perceptions of the Dragon Blooded and even influence of the Immaculate Philosophy are things that are much older than the Realm.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Dragon Blooded Shogunate ruled the entire world in a much more literal manner than the Realm does, and even though that <i>still</i> would have been a time where there weren't enough Dragon Blooded for everybody to be personal witnesses to them, their influence would have been much more evenly spread out. The Immaculate Philosophy was not as strong (which may have just amounted to them not having an organised and hierarchical body that was actually part of the ruling establishment), but they'll still have been spread over many parts of the world, repeating the narrative of the dangerous and unworthy Solars and Lunars.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo I would say that overall, the people of Ysyr think of the Dragon Blooded as much of the world does; the Exalted, the legendary rulers of the world (even if in practical terms that mostly means that they're somewhere off in the distance being a tremendously rich ultimate destination for local trade goods and possibly ultimate source for certain sorcerous reagents and instruments that Ysyr will have a peculiar market for), who saved the world from the Fair Folk way back when.<br /> <br /> \u200bI would suppose that if they meet an actual outcaste, they'll recognise abstractly that this is the same kind of person as those legends, but in more grounded terms. Mostly just &quot;this is somebody worth a bit of respect, and with strengths meaning that they need to be approached carefully&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bI can picture their attitudes towards the rulers of neighbouring Prasad as even more abstractly considering them to be Exalted, and otherwise more firmly rooted into the politics of the ongoing competition.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think most people in the world follow the general course of the Anathema narrative regardless of what they take from Immaculate spirituality, because the narrative about them being extremely dangerous has been heavily promulgated, and is extremely credible in any (usually Lunars) happen to do anything nearby.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, in relative terms, Ma-Ha-Suchi is <i>right over there</i>. He's a lot better than he was in Second Edition, but I'd say that even distant familiarity with him paints him as a terrifying person. More of a slumbering and easily placated dragon than just another local ruler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T18:04:49-08:00","id":1052310,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that given how distanced Prasad's version of the Immaculate practices are from the baseline, and Ysyr being even farther from the Blessed Isle, its understanding of their teachings would be even more remote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T19:07:53-08:00","id":1052342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052297#post1052297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'mma have to disagree with the assertion that it's academic. There's a pretty significant difference between &quot;This thing is powerful and I should be very careful around it,&quot; vs &quot;This thing is a demon from Hell that is going to try to eat my soul and I should find someone to help me kill it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant the distinction to a non-Immaculate between the powerful and dangerous Solar &amp; Lunar Anathema and the powerful and dangerous Solar &amp; Lunar Exalted is largely academic. Because either way, they are often quite dangerous and regardless of the lens that you interpret their actions through, they still often represent a threat to the status quo.<br /> <br /> But I think that's really secondary to the point, which is that Immaculate or no, I was suggesting there would be a clear recognition of the danger that these beings from the Immaculate fables represent. Whether they see that as &quot;opportunity&quot; or &quot;trouble&quot; is as likely to vary by the individual as it is for any other Thresholder not beholden to Immaculate ideology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T01:02:06-08:00","id":1052437,"title":"","content":"I don't think Ysyr has native DBs, at least not in any number. Ysyr is stated to be &quot;pitting their forces against Volivat and Prasad, so I doubt they think very highly of the Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Prasad, and the geographic distance between it and the Realm, I imagine that most inhabitants of Prasad are barely aware of the Realm's existence. The Dragon-Blooded know more about it, but probably still view themselves as only nominally affiliated with their distant cousins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T01:59:14-08:00","id":1052460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052291#post1052291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something about this initial question feels very strange to me, since it seems to assume that places having a noteworthy group of Dragon Blooded is the norm.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's very much the tone that was set by Exalted: The Outcastes where rather than focusing on attitudes and potential sources of Terrestrial Bloodlines it kind of assumes everywhere has a thriving Dragon-Blooded community unless it got poached by the Realm or wiped out. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T05:12:52-08:00","id":1052507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052291#post1052291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI think on the one occasion where somebody from Ysyr Exalted as anything about five hundred years ago, if that person didn't already want to become a sorcerer in order to integrate smoothly into the existing class structure, then the thaumatocrats elaborated some highly specific social and legal terminology to describe the one Exalt who happened there ever as belonging to some kind of category distinct from the usual caste system without actually undermining it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like exactly the kind of thing a small ruling class might do. I could imagine a traditional exceptional social role reserved for the once in a generation Outcaste that Exalts in Ysyr. Some kind of champion or other dramatic role. It could be of genuine aid to the sorcerers as a unique person in the system. It could also potentially provide an easy way for them to get rid of said outcastes, sending them away on some great impossible mission for the city or sending them to their death. Maybe both have happened over the course of Ysyr's existence!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T05:30:11-08:00","id":1052513,"title":"","content":"I kind of don't have much to say about the Dragonblooded that hasn't been said, but a couple thoughts on a couple parts of OP:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded#post1052247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She suggested to me that she actually doesn't have an inherent problem with the Solar Exalted, and figured that her view of them was that they were ancient powerful and enlightened people, with all the risks that go along with that sort of thing... but no view of them as Anathema or evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think makes sense although on another tack - they could have good occult lore and trafficking with demons and gods, they are probably aware of the end of the First Age, and have some awareness of late First Age horrors / atrocities. That could go with believing that the Solars turned to evil, albeit not looking at this through the Immaculate Philosophy's lens of Anathema.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded#post1052247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She reasoned that that Ys probably have no use for the Immaculates</div> </div> </div> </div>Be interested to know what your player has to say about how she views her character's religious beliefs and thinking about the gods, and whether she sees there as being gods of Ysyr who matter to it, or it as a godless society.<br /> <br /> My intuition would be a pragmatism about the gods. IRC there's not anything like a harmonious relationship with a local court of gods (like An Teng's Golden Lord, Ahlat's position in much of the South, etc.), or a relationship with Heaven as a feature of Ysyr society in the brief description we have. That might go hand in hand with suspicion of any Exalt who approaches things as a champion of a god (Exigent, a Solar with this perspective, etc.).<br /> <br /> Although equally, they could probably accommodate a strong relationship with a local god or gods as a patron or equal, if you wanted to include that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T06:10:01-08:00","id":1052527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052460#post1052460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's very much the tone that was set by Exalted: The Outcastes where rather than focusing on attitudes and potential sources of Terrestrial Bloodlines it kind of assumes everywhere has a thriving Dragon-Blooded community unless it got poached by the Realm or wiped out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI mean... I'll agree that it probably wasn't the best idea for a supplement that presents itself as being about the average Dragon Blooded outside of the Realm to devote half of its content to describing the large groups and a quarter to what happens to Outcastes within the Realm, but I would find that to be different from a presentation of everywhere in the world having its own Forest Witches.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm going to assume that &quot;sources of Terrestrial bloodlines&quot; is referring to places where Exaltation might be disproportionately common.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T06:21:01-08:00","id":1052532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052460#post1052460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's very much the tone that was set by Exalted: The Outcastes where rather than focusing on attitudes and potential sources of Terrestrial Bloodlines it kind of assumes everywhere has a thriving Dragon-Blooded community unless it got poached by the Realm or wiped out.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I wouldn't use the term thriving, I would in fact suggest that Terrestrial bloodlines are (while uncommon) not difficult to find over pretty much the entire population. I just think those Outcaste are going to be culturally removed from the Realm entirely. Yser may have a Terrestrial family or three. I just doubt they'd care about what the Realm is or spend any time understanding it. Given that the High First Age saw very high mobility, the same justification that allows for the blended ethnic background of many regions of Creation pretty much ensures you'll find Lost Eggs even in the most remote locations.<br /> <br /> This is part of the reason why I think the 1e/2e canon approach to Terrestrial - Lunar relations... that of a 'splat-war' ala the Salubri/Tremere... is pretty silly. Lunar Exalted would have numerous communities of Terrestrial bloodlines that would have no allegiance to the Realm at all. So I view the idea of Terrestrial Exalted as the 'trump card' of the Sidereal Exalted as being pretty stupid.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm sure the Realm has by far the most influential and well provisioned group of Dragonblooded. That's not difficult at all for me to buy. Creation is huge, however - I assure you that Dragonblooded empires exist in many, many places that have no idea what the Realm is and no allegiance to it. Suggesting anything else tends too far towards 2e 'collapsing the world', where everything feels next door and the world seems like it's as big as a state more or less.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T06:30:18-08:00","id":1052535,"title":"","content":"I think the sorcerous powers of the thaumatocrats and their ability to enslave the raksha probably put them in a position where Gods might be wary of them or unwilling/uninterested in sharing information in detail about times like the First Age.<br /> <br /> That isn't to say that they couldn't get such information, I just think it's probably a safer/more interesting assumption to go with the idea that they're not terribly well-informed by the weird first-hand accounts that Gods may or may not give of things like the Solars.<br /> <br /> It really does come down to what your player from Ysyr is thinking, though. I think she's right on the money in rationalizing that Ysyr probably doesn't have an inherent issue with the Solars, but that they have the appropriate caution that any individual dealing with powerful beings exhibits.<br /> <br /> Though as a side note, I would feel inclined to think that there's been at <i>least </i>one Pure Way monk that's been over to Ysyr or otherwise been engaged by Ysyr for knowledge of things like the Anathema and the like.<br /> <br /> This should all be contextualized by stuff like how they might have more direct experience with the Lunar Exalted, and that it's probable that in the past, the Ys people or the people who would become the seafaring Ys were exposed to the Immaculate doctrine and ideas of the Shogunate at some point.<br /> <br /> So the idea is probably not an alien one, even if it's not something they particularly buy into at this point. I definitely think they'll have much stronger feelings about Lunars because they've likely encountered Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T07:19:08-08:00","id":1052555,"title":"","content":"Full disclosure: I play in this game, but I am not the player in question.<br /> <br /> I think Levi has a good point, here. The cultural heritage of Creation as a whole is the Shogunate, and fear of the Anathema is drawn from that well, regardless of whether or not a given culture has much contact with current Immaculates or the Realm. The Wyld Hunt in Ex3 is mentioned as being explicitly a Dragon-Blooded institution, rather than a Realm one. It's a bit like the disparate cultures of Dark Ages Europe all valuing Latin and drawing from Roman culture in various ways.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, Ysyr may not believe in &quot;Anathema&quot; but it's highly unlikely they have a positive opinion of Celestial Exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T07:34:43-08:00","id":1052560,"title":"","content":"Cool! I hope you guys have fun in your game. My group is also playing in the Dreaming Sea right now! As a small note of clarification, I think the passage you're referencing describes both the specific organization called the Wyld Hunt in the Realm, and also the social institution present in most places with Dragon-Blooded which describes rounding up a posse to go deal with a big bad thing.<br /> <br /> I imagine if anything that the Ys might have an easier time with Shogunate scholarship of these things than First Age, unless Pinnacle itself yielded more to them, which can be cool too. It sounds like a fun situation for a PC to Exalt in and have to figure out, 'what now?'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T07:42:03-08:00","id":1052565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052560#post1052560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool! I hope you guys have fun in your game. My group is also playing in the Dreaming Sea right now! As a small note of clarification, I think the passage you're referencing describes both the specific organization called the Wyld Hunt in the Realm, and also the social institution present in most places with Dragon-Blooded which describes rounding up a posse to go deal with a big bad thing.<br /> <br /> I imagine if anything that the Ys might have an easier time with Shogunate scholarship of these things than First Age, unless Pinnacle itself yielded more to them, which can be cool too. It sounds like a fun situation for a PC to Exalt in and have to figure out, 'what now?'</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely love the Dreaming Sea, but unfortunately the game doesn't point there at this particular moment. The Ys Sorcerer has already joined the party in the Scavenger Lands, and we are about to gallivant in the South a bit. This thread is really more about discovering/discussing the likely feelings of the PC and her servants about her situation.<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible Pinnacle yield more First Age secrets, but then I think raw pragmatism would still rule the day, as you suggested. Celestial Exalts are powerful, long-lived, and ambitious. It doesn't benefit the ruling the class to simply ignore them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T07:52:55-08:00","id":1052570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052555#post1052555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyld Hunt in Ex3 is mentioned as being explicitly a Dragon-Blooded institution, rather than a Realm one.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's a detail I quite liked; it gave me a sense that the communal aspect of the Dragon Blooded is something that continues to function without needing every single Dragon Blood to belong to an explicit community. That the legacy of their worldwide rule and the continuing prominence of a particular group means that they form the standard for the term &quot;Exalted&quot; across the world, meaning that any given Exalt has a background that informs them that they're part of something bigger with certain obligations even if they never even meet another Terrestrial.<br /> <br /> \u200bI've got this idea where even without adherents to the actual Immaculate faiths*, there's a widely exported narrative that identifies the Realm to the world's Dragon Blooded as being the highest and finest example of the Exalted making good on their potential and their obligations. That a lot of the world's Exalted are encouraged to look in on it as an example to live up to.<br /> <br /> \u200bI imagine that the Sidereals and their allies in Heaven are helping a bit to spread and cement this narrative even outside of the most direct reach of the Realm.<br /> <br /> \u200bSomething I would especially like about all of this is that it would present a basis for secret bloodlines of Terrestrial Exalted who are subservient to the Lunars and integral to their plans to not really be a thing, because I don't particularly like it.<br /> <br /> \u200bWell, all of that and maybe the idea that a lot of Lunars have formed certain trust issues regarding the question of being nominal leader of a large number of Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that in mind, Ysyr may not believe in &quot;Anathema&quot; but it's highly unlikely they have a positive opinion of Celestial Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'm also going to be interested in how this Edition will likely play up how to most of the world, Anathema means &quot;Lunar Exalted&quot;, as well as how a lot of the Lunars have not been giving the brand a lot of good publicity.<br /> <br /> \u200b* Using this as a descriptive term rather than a specifically defined piece of the lexicon and I swear to God if one person comes and &quot;Um, actually&quot; to me about it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T08:03:28-08:00","id":1052576,"title":"","content":"Regarding the matter of how there's a society ruled by Dragon Blooded (who are apparently either something like a disconnected colony of the Realm or another enclave of Shogunate influences) proverbially next door to Ysyr, I think something analogous to my idea about a certain dissonance between their abstract notions of the Exalted and their actual political relations with them would be a lot of situations in pre-modern and early modern Europe involving the relations between kings and certain subjects, or kings and the pope.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you're a powerful noble in a European kingdom of the time, you might maintain the narrative that the king is God's special creature in an overall sense, you're just a bit insistent that the king stay over there and not interfere in your administration of your own property, or infringe on your aristocratic rights. You're not fighting to replace the king, you're fighting to make the king sign the great charter of your liberties.<br /> <br /> I'd say that Ysyr can oppose Prasad in terms of a <i>very emphatic</i> insistence that they can get by on their own and don't require any of the assistance of the Exalted <i>oblige</i>. A &quot;thanks, but no thanks&quot; spelled out with massed ranks of spears. Or occasionally even an assertion that while those Exalted have legitimacy, they're overstepping their bounds a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T08:14:12-08:00","id":1052580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052570#post1052570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Using this as a descriptive term rather than a specifically defined piece of the lexicon and I swear to God if one person comes and &quot;Um, actually&quot; to me about it\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, actually I was going to ask why you still had an <i>Adventure Time</i> sig, but have switched to a <i>Steven Universe</i> avatar. I'm sure Pearl's got some great quotes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T08:27:20-08:00","id":1052581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052576#post1052576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the matter of how there's a society ruled by Dragon Blooded (who are apparently either something like a disconnected colony of the Realm or another enclave of Shogunate influences) proverbially next door to Ysyr, I think something analogous to my idea about a certain dissonance between their abstract notions of the Exalted and their actual political relations with them would be a lot of situations in pre-modern and early modern Europe involving the relations between kings and certain subjects, or kings and the pope.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you're a powerful noble in a European kingdom of the time, you might maintain the narrative that the king is God's special creature in an overall sense, you're just a bit insistent that the king stay over there and not interfere in your administration of your own property, or infringe on your aristocratic rights. You're not fighting to replace the king, you're fighting to make the king sign the great charter of your liberties.<br /> <br /> I'd say that Ysyr can oppose Prasad in terms of a <i>very emphatic</i> insistence that they can get by on their own and don't require any of the assistance of the Exalted <i>oblige</i>. A &quot;thanks, but no thanks&quot; spelled out with massed ranks of spears. Or occasionally even an assertion that while those Exalted have legitimacy, they're overstepping their bounds a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes sense to me. It's a bit like the stories of George Washington toasting to the King's health during the Revolutionary War. He and his officers figured they would fight for a bit, an agreement would be reached, and they could continue as loyal subjects. Similarly, European Kings often made a big deal of being completely loyal to the Church while simultaneously opposing the current Pope's policies.<br /> <br /> I don't know if this is strictly necessary, though. I could see the ruling class of Ysyr deliberately cultivating a culture that doesn't inherently respect the Dragon-Blooded over time. Reverence for the Exalted can be replaced with reverence for Sorcerers. To me, this seems dependent on how long Prasad and Ysyr have been fighting. if the Dreaming Sea's post-Contagion/Crusade history is defined by on-going conflict, it's unlikely the deference to the Chosen has endured.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if shifting geopolitical winds cause the powers to sometimes make peace and other times make war, a complex cultural situation could emerge. Those in Ysyr who benefit from peaceful relations favor the Dragon-Blooded, while those who profit from war (or at least don't profit during peace) tend to emphasize autonomy/patriotism/jingoism. It's a bit like the political situation in the United States currently. Those who economically benefit from open migration and globalization tend to support it, and those who have lost out on the economic gains tend to oppose it. <br /> <br /> Regardless, I don't see Ysyr discarding distrust/fear of Anathema. They have empirical evidence to support that bias, and competent rulers rarely encourage competing power centers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T08:37:05-08:00","id":1052583,"title":"","content":"While I don't disagree with you, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6601_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6601\" data-vbnamecard=\"6601\">Totentanz</a>, current events suggest that the mere presence of overwhelming empirical evidence is just not gonna be enough for some people.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wouldn't it be great if we could just get along with Anathema?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I respect the Anathema. They're killers? Do you think Ysyr is so innocent?&quot;<br /> <br /> Arrrgh, why is this happening?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T09:07:26-08:00","id":1052595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052581#post1052581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if this is strictly necessary, though. I could see the ruling class of Ysyr deliberately cultivating a culture that doesn't inherently respect the Dragon-Blooded over time. Reverence for the Exalted can be replaced with reverence for Sorcerers. To me, this seems dependent on how long Prasad and Ysyr have been fighting. if the Dreaming Sea's post-Contagion/Crusade history is defined by on-going conflict, it's unlikely the deference to the Chosen has endured.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat sounds good.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, think about in that case if instances in which the occasional Dragon Blood pops up amongst their own has them utilise a kind of synthesis of old narratives about the Exalted and the current pre-eminence of sorcerers, such that an Exalted sorcerer in their midst is a kind of special refinement or divinely ordained one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T10:13:57-08:00","id":1052615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052576#post1052576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the matter of how there's a society ruled by Dragon Blooded (who are apparently either something like a disconnected colony of the Realm or another enclave of Shogunate influences) proverbially next door to Ysyr, I think something analogous to my idea about a certain dissonance between their abstract notions of the Exalted and their actual political relations with them would be a lot of situations in pre-modern and early modern Europe involving the relations between kings and certain subjects, or kings and the pope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right next door? They are 3,700 miles distance from each other!<br /> <br /> That's bigger than the distance between New York and London!<br /> <br /> I think the community is having a real hard time grasping the scale of the 3e map. The Dreaming Sea begins to feel like a really big lake when you take the cities that adjoin it as a list of NPC factions that are all interacting. It's not a really big lake. It's a sea. It's fuckin' huge.<br /> <br /> This was a huge problem in 2e. The world became very small. A similar issue happened with Demons, Spirits and Elementals - the few canonical examples intended to represent a slice of a vast spiritual ecosystem became the flora and fauna of the world almost exclusively. Many, many kingdoms of similar stature, history and weirdness exist between Y'syr and Prasad. They are in no way 'next door'.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T10:31:00-08:00","id":1052626,"title":"","content":"The thing is this is not the community doing this here exactly - the book says <i>&quot;The sorcerers (of Ysyr) continue to extend their influence, pitting their forces against the preternatural champions of Volivat, the Dragon-Blooded princes of Prasad, and the other imperial powers of the Dreaming Sea.&quot;</i> You would presume this means they are actually interacting, competing, warring. I would expect from what you say about distance this would likely be more &quot;The Great Game&quot; than literally in one another's face but I don't know that's incompatible with the kind of influence Levi's talking about.<br /> <br /> Likewise I would say this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052285#post1052285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Yser? I'd FULLY support them being virtually untouched by Realm authority, and possibly even removed enough to say sincerely, 'Wait, what 'Realm' are you talking about?'. I prefer a huge world with isolated cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm down with what you're looking for from my preference, but the 3e book seem to describe a world where the Dragonblooded's boot is up in everyone's face (and noticeably more so than in the 1e main book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T11:33:48-08:00","id":1052654,"title":"","content":"I think that passage is poorly considered and an example of the 'Dreaming Sea as a Lake' perception.<br /> <br /> I mean, let's be clear - as per the scale of the new map, we're dealing with a distance that's as great as that between BEIJING and EGYPT.<br /> <br /> I like the new world and scale, because it enriches the 3e setting, but I think the fiction has thus far been unfortunately... inconsistent, on being faithful to the idea of such a vast world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T12:01:10-08:00","id":1052676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052654#post1052654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, let's be clear - as per the scale of the new map, we're dealing with a distance that's as great as that between BEIJING and EGYPT.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the distances are somewhat similar, but as has been noted elsewhere, the ancients were capable of voyages of these sorts of lengths, ages before folks like us assumed they were able to do so. Moreover, <i>un</i>like the ancients, people in Creation already know there's lands and people out there, with shiny things to go and trade with them for, because in ages past, the Solars went out and tamed the world.<br /> <br /> I mean, let's say some ignorant asshole in charge of everything decides to start a pointless nuclear war that wipes out most of humanity, leading to a new dark age as our glorious tech breaks down over the years and generations without the vast support networks to maintain it all; do you think that people in Africa, North America, Australia, et cetera., would suddenly forget <i>Asia exists</i> and not try and send people over there to see what's going on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-21-2017, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T13:51:27-08:00","id":1052743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052654#post1052654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that passage is poorly considered and an example of the 'Dreaming Sea as a Lake' perception.<br /> <br /> I mean, let's be clear - as per the scale of the new map, we're dealing with a distance that's as great as that between BEIJING and EGYPT.<br /> <br /> I like the new world and scale, because it enriches the 3e setting, but I think the fiction has thus far been unfortunately... inconsistent, on being faithful to the idea of such a vast world.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in the real world, there were Africans and Israelites (if that is the proper term. Judeans? I dunno) in Roman Britain, Roman-made trade goods found in Japan, Europeans in Tang-Dynasty China, and Norse fishermen in the New World, etc.<br /> <br /> While it wasn't very common, there was international/intercontinental migration of people, goods and ideas throughout human history, up to and including the Stone Ages. <br /> <br /> I mean, hell, the Roman and Han Empires coexisted and considered each other approximate equals, receiving and giving tribute.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:02:00-08:00","id":1052753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052654#post1052654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that passage is poorly considered and an example of the 'Dreaming Sea as a Lake' perception.<br /> <br /> I mean, let's be clear - as per the scale of the new map, we're dealing with a distance that's as great as that between BEIJING and EGYPT.<br /> <br /> I like the new world and scale, because it enriches the 3e setting, but I think the fiction has thus far been unfortunately... inconsistent, on being faithful to the idea of such a vast world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many also ignore how far shorter distances actually are with pre-modern technology in terms of personal travel, poltical relationships and cultural penetration[1]. Even if we shrink the map scale so Ysyr and Prasad are as Spain and Anatolia, we can still fit dozens or hundreds of distinct societies between them in our ancient-to-early modern Mediterranean to whom these distant powers are typically a far lesser consideration than their local rivals, even as they vie for influence with hard and soft power. Recall that to the Ancient Greeks, the Ten Thousand's march from Babylon to Greece was an epic journey through an essentially alien world, and that's around 2000km. Of course, it's a fantasy setting and there are are some individuals who can break these rules wide open, but they're extremely rare, even among exalts[2]. Enough that these things can be significant to the epic narratives of Exalted PCs, but not enough to transform societal dynamics.<br /> <br /> Orthogonally, while I agree that Immaculate ideas have significant influence (if rarely <i>primacy</i>) well beyond the borders of The Realm, I think most people vastly overestimate the importance of the Anathema to Immaculate belief. Understandably so, since mosts PCs are such &quot;Anathema&quot;, but the beliefs about the conception of society as the Perfected Hierarchy, the proper relationship between mortals and spirits, the cycle of reincarnation, and the occult practice of ritual, are all surely far more central to both the belief and praxis of Immaculates and Immaculate-influenced believers across creation[3].<br /> <br /> [1] <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/AskHistorians/comments/5uxw9b/where_there_tribes_still_in_the_stone_age_in_the/\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> reddit AskHistorians post has a nice description of how &quot;Chinese&quot; culture failed to penetrate the interior until surprisingly late. Unmentioned, but equally pertinent, would be Taiwan -- a mere 200km off the coast, but not brought into the Chinese sphere until the 17th century.<br /> [2] There's almost nothing in the Solar charmset that achieves this, maybe a Ride charm or two. Otherwise we're talking about Sorcerors who take Stormwind Rider, and maybe some artefacts.<br /> [3] I'd liken the place anathema, for most immaculate believers, to that of the apocalypse in the Abrahamic faiths. For some people and some sects it's of central importance, but it just doesn't matter on an everyday basis to most Catholics or conventional Sunnis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12943-handigar","name":"Handigar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:04:19-08:00","id":1052756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052615#post1052615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right next door? They are 3,700 miles distance from each other!<br /> <br /> That's bigger than the distance between New York and London!</div> </div> </div> </div> :nods: That's almost the distance from Kamthahar to Chiaroscuro.<br /> <br /> Although the terrain along the westwards trail in a lot rougher and I expect Prasad stretches eastwards towards the coast, has fingers in trade routes to the south east, and such, simultaneously exclaiming \u200b&quot;They're unimaginably distant from the Realm,&quot; and &quot;They're right on Ysyr's doorstep,&quot; is still a bit of a disconnect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 02-21-2017, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:06:08-08:00","id":1052757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052743#post1052743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And in the real world, there were Africans and Israelites (if that is the proper term. Judeans? I dunno) in Roman Britain, Roman-made trade goods found in Japan, Europeans in Tang-Dynasty China, and Norse fishermen in the New World, etc.<br /> <br /> While it wasn't very common, there was international/intercontinental migration of people, goods and ideas throughout human history, up to and including the Stone Ages.<br /> <br /> I mean, hell, the Roman and Han Empires coexisted and considered each other approximate equals, receiving and giving tribute.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They knew each other existed, but very few individuals ever saw both Rome and Chang'an. The Romans <i>may</i> have sent one embassy in the second century AD, and the closest any recorded Chinese official got was Persia, where he gave up after the locals lied about the distances involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12943-handigar","name":"Handigar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:41:26-08:00","id":1052788,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if the contact between Ysyr and Prasad was handled like the contact between Rome and the Han, that would be one thing. But they are described as being competing imperial powers, which is just... not really at all feasible, given the distances involved. Real empires who were that distant from each other didn't really have those kind of relationships until the modern era. Silk Road trade and mysterious legends are totally fine, but direct military conflict and power struggles? Very difficult to suspend disbelief given difficulty in both communication, and transportation. The logistics alone...<br /> <br /> I love the new map scale and the implied vast creative space conjured up by expanding it, but it feels like a cheap gimmick of the authors keep writing as though Creation is 1/10th of the size it is said to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:08:50-08:00","id":1052812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052654#post1052654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, let's be clear - as per the scale of the new map, we're dealing with a distance that's as great as that between BEIJING and EGYPT.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sooooo Egypt; as in, what was once a province of the Abbasid caliphate.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd Beijing, as in what was once a member of the Tang Dynasty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">they are described as being competing imperial powers, which is just... not really at all feasible, given the distances involved. Real empires who were that distant from each other didn't really have those kind of relationships until the modern era.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Talas\" target=\"_blank\">they didn't do it very often</a>.<br /> <br /> \u200bOne side has Exalted and the other has sorcerers. I find it plausible enough that they can conduct such warfare a bit more consistently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:14:19-08:00","id":1052815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052788#post1052788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if the contact between Ysyr and Prasad was handled like the contact between Rome and the Han, that would be one thing. But they are described as being competing imperial powers, which is just... not really at all feasible, given the distances involved. Real empires who were that distant from each other didn't really have those kind of relationships until the modern era. Silk Road trade and mysterious legends are totally fine, but direct military conflict and power struggles? Very difficult to suspend disbelief given difficulty in both communication, and transportation. The logistics alone...<br /> <br /> I love the new map scale and the implied vast creative space conjured up by expanding it, but it feels like a cheap gimmick of the authors keep writing as though Creation is 1/10th of the size it is said to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>My preference is to take inspiration from the map as drawn, and then move the most intersting canon locations around so they can plausibly interact. My game is set in the Dreaming Sea, but Lookshy no lies on it's northern shores and the centre of the Scarlet Empire has been relocated to the former Scavenger Lands so that the Grey River, guarded by half a dozen embattled Satrapies, can form a tenuous line of communication to Prasad. That said, all dozen sessions so far[1] have been set on that big island south-east of Champoor (we call it Lujira).<br /> <br /> With that in mind, though Ysyr is off our campaign map to the south-east, it could well be close enough that Prasadi and Ys commercial interests and soft power intersect, leading to hostility and low-intensity conflict, rather than Rome/Carthage style rivalry. It certainly pales in comparison to the internal rivalries between different Prasadi houses and the the same with the Imperial Exarchate. Both Dragonblooded and sorcerors may have rather more strategic mobility than armies or fleets, leading to the individual clashes noted in the book, but any Prasadi invasion of Ysyr would be an expedition comparable to those of Ban Chao, Aelius Gallus or Alexander.<br /> <br /> [1] Excluding the Exaltation sessions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12943-handigar","name":"Handigar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:20:31-08:00","id":1052824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052812#post1052812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOne side has Exalted and the other has sorcerers. I find it plausible enough that they can conduct such warfare a bit more consistently.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why would they even fight? The fact that a person can Stormwind Rider over there doesn't mean that they have any competing interests. Rome didn't engage in those kind of behaviors with the Chinese. They sent tribute and made nice but that was about trade, not military issues... no Roman seriously expected the Chinese would be coming over the mountain anytime soon, or challenging them for dominion of Greece or Egypt. Even if they COULD, by virtue of some strange sorcery, send supernatural diplomats over there... they still wouldn't be interested in the various geopolitical affairs of each other. It's just not relevant.<br /> <br /> Secondly to that, from a purely game design standpoint, what does shrinking the world gain us? I find the Dreaming Sea much more interesting than the Dreaming Lake.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:38:02-08:00","id":1052843,"title":"","content":"You keep saying &quot;lake&quot; but I think I'm looking at this the preconception of &quot;sea&quot; here to be about the size of the Mediterranean or the North Sea or the Gulf of Mexico+Caribbean Sea, with similar political dynamics around it, and it seems to me that's what the name suggests. Not really either a lake or an ocean (though the Indian Ocean feels like the best ocean to model on if there is one to be taken). Though you're saying it's not much like any of those seas and its oceanic vastness would imply little or no contact (so unlike the Mediterranean..).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:49:23-08:00","id":1052856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052824#post1052824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But why would they even fight? The fact that a person can Stormwind Rider over there doesn't mean that they have any competing interests. Rome didn't engage in those kind of behaviors with the Chinese. They sent tribute and made nice but that was about trade, not military issues... no Roman seriously expected the Chinese would be coming over the mountain anytime soon, or challenging them for dominion of Greece or Egypt. Even if they COULD, by virtue of some strange sorcery, send supernatural diplomats over there... they still wouldn't be interested in the various geopolitical affairs of each other. It's just not relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are you talking about Romans and Chinese when I'm linking to a page describing a battle <i>that actually happened</i> between Muslims and Chinese?<br /> <br /> \u200bWhy did the Abbasid Muslims and Tang Chinese fight over cultural hegemony in Kazakhstan? To have pre-eminence in the trade, and probably for a bit of an ideological aspect (possibly more so on the part of the Abbasids than the Tang, although that's a dynasty I'm less familiar with).<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough even regarding Rome, Roman eastward expansion conceivably <i>could</i> have continued until they made contact with Chinese expansion had it not been for the fact that the Parthian and then.. was it Selucid or Sassanid... the Sassanid empire kept being in the way and kept winning when Romans tried to expand east. And Rome probably would have kept expanding east if it could, given things like needing to find land for its retiring soldiers, and how much the ridiculously wealthy aristocracy depended on provinces to acquire that ridiculous wealth, or just the fact that Rome itself also had a cultural ideology based on their superiority and right to conquer the world.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr hell, maybe it's as simple as one side of the other having an equivalent to Alexander of Macedon who goes around saying &quot;there was a comet on the day I was born, so I'm going to conquer continuously until I reach the local equivalent of the Himalayas because I want it&quot;, except this time he or she or they has advantages such as a constitution that doesn't die from overdrinking in its early thirties and a bit more administrative talent, so that territory can actually last a bit longer, and then you follow through with the original plans to <i>keep moving east</i> because this time you can raise an army that won't mutiny over the prospect because you can get them over to the frontier without having to spend ten years fighting to get there.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr maybe they just stay there for a few hundred years and then the local equivalent to the Tang dynasty happens, and they get very peeved at the existence of this stable empire standing in the way of their expansion west.<br /> <br /> It's really not difficult to think of reasons why such expansion would be relevant.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, I was thinking about what the capabilities of the Exalted and sorcery for large scale warfare and administration might be, not sending over individuals. Considering the fact that real life people without sorcery have been able to effectively govern territories the size of, well, the Tang dynasty (or the Song dynasty, or the Ming dynasty, or the Qing dynasty) back when the most advanced piece of long range communications technology was the horse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly to that, from a purely game design standpoint, what does shrinking the world gain us? I find the Dreaming Sea much more interesting than the Dreaming Lake.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't find the description of the empires surrounding the Dreaming Sea to make it feel like a small place; I feel like it sounds like a very big place involving lots of different kinds of people who happen to be caught up in battles for supremacy between a few of the more powerful ones. Describing places such as Palanquin helps with that; it makes it feel as though Macedon-ruled Afghanistan is a very different place to actual Macedonia.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:58:20-08:00","id":1052867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052788#post1052788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real empires who were that distant from each other didn't really have those kind of relationships until the modern era. Silk Road trade and mysterious legends are totally fine, but direct military conflict and power struggles? Very difficult to suspend disbelief given difficulty in both communication, and transportation. The logistics alone...</div> </div> </div> </div>As you note, real empires that distant from each other in the real world had lots of inhospitable terrain between them. Offhand, I can't think of two ancient empires connected by a sufficiently long stretch of populous, mostly linear coastline to draw a viable comparison. Meanwhile, Alexander the Great led his troops almost 4,000 miles from Macedonia to northern India \u2014 a far more difficult transit, performed without the peculiar benefits accessible to Creation's heroes and warlords. More applicably, Rome and Persia warred intermittently for close to seven centuries, with capitals close to 2,000 miles apart as the crow flies, or close to 3,000 miles apart in terms of actual travel distance.<br /> <br /> (Speaking of Alexander, the Indo-Greek Kingdom is good cultural inspiration for Prasad's divergence from the Realm.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T16:14:37-08:00","id":1052878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052867#post1052867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you note, real empires that distant from each other in the real world had lots of inhospitable terrain between them. Offhand, I can't think of two ancient empires connected by a sufficiently long stretch of populous, mostly linear coastline to draw a viable comparison</div> </div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> Perhaps we should think about South-East Asia, with populous urban civilization stretching from Guangdong around the bend of Vietnam to Thailand, Malaysia and Indonesia?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More applicably, Rome and Persia warred intermittently for close to seven centuries, with capitals close to 2,000 miles apart as the crow flies, or close to 3,000 miles apart in terms of actual travel distance. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but however far apart the capitals, two of the most populous and wealthy provinces of each empire shared a border on the Euphrates. How long did it take for the ripples of Talas to diffuse into the currents of history, overwhelmed by the storm of the Abbasid Revolution and the An Lushan rebellion?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Speaking of Alexander, the Indo-Greek Kingdom is good cultural inspiration for Prasad's divergence from the Realm.) </div> </div> </div>I love this, though my model so far has been Nan Yue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12943-handigar","name":"Handigar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T16:39:10-08:00","id":1052894,"title":"","content":"<br /> Prasad/Ysyr really reminds me of Paragon and Gem back in 1st edition and 2nd edition. In fact, the distance between Ysyr and Parasad's capital are about the same as the distance between Gem and Paragon. Back during 2nd edition it was generally agreed that Gem and Paragon were too far apart to realistically engage in a trade war with one another, let alone an actual military conflict. Admittedly the harsh desert environment was an important factor, but just the sheer distance alone between the nations played a big role in making people wonder how these two states would end up at odds with one another.<br /> <br /> While it is absolutely possible to imagine Paragon (or Prasad) gathering up an army to march on Gem/Ysyr (or vice versa) such an event should probably be presented as a monumental and exceptional undertaking, even in the Exalted setting, comparable to Alexander's march across the world (there's a reason we're still talking about his accomplishment 1700 years later). It feel's a little odd to have it just tossed out there as a matter of course, similar to how the Gem/Paragon conflict felt odd for being tossed out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T16:56:09-08:00","id":1052905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052894#post1052894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">comparable to Alexander's march across the world (there's a reason we're still talking about his accomplishment 1700 years later).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we talk about Alexander's achievement because he had really good press.<br /> <br /> \u200bForming empires that are several thousand miles long is surprisingly common throughout history, but a lot of them just don't get discussed in the popular consciousness.<br /> <br /> \u200bHave you ever heard of the G\u00f6kt\u00fcrk Khaganate? <br /> <br /> \u200bI think Gem and Paragon were odd because they were city-states based in an arid region, compared to places that are described as expansionistic imperial powers in a lush environment with the addition of maritime transport.<br /> <br /> \u200bDo you want to know what you get out of the Dreaming Sea rather than the Dreaming Lake? Maritime trade links connecting Arabia with Indonesia.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T16:58:46-08:00","id":1052908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052894#post1052894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prasad/Ysyr really reminds me of Paragon and Gem back in 1st edition and 2nd edition. In fact, the distance between Ysyr and Parasad's capital are about the same as the distance between Gem and Paragon. Back during 2nd edition it was generally agreed that Gem and Paragon were too far apart to realistically engage in a trade war with one another, let alone an actual military conflict. Admittedly the harsh desert environment was an important factor, but just the sheer distance alone between the nations played a big role in making people wonder how these two states would end up at odds with one another.<br /> <br /> While it is absolutely possible to imagine Paragon (or Prasad) gathering up an army to march on Gem/Ysyr (or vice versa) such an event should probably be presented as a monumental and exceptional undertaking, even in the Exalted setting, comparable to Alexander's march across the world (there's a reason we're still talking about his accomplishment 1700 years later). It feel's a little odd to have it just tossed out there as a matter of course, similar to how the Gem/Paragon conflict felt odd for being tossed out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prasad and Ysyr are imperial powers. Though they are of course far smaller and weaker than the Realm itself, they are, to my understanding, significantly richer, more populous, and more militarily powerful than any published Threshold state under Realm dominion. In matters of scale and realpolitik, they are more akin to the Realm than they are to city-states like Gem and Paragon.<br /> <br /> This goes against how the Threshold has long been depicted, but that's a large part of the narrative role of the Dreaming Sea \u2014 to provide an arena for imperial play at sufficient remove from the Blessed Isle that it takes place outside the shadow of the Realm, while still fitting into Creation proper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:04:36-08:00","id":1052912,"title":"","content":"So like, does Prasad actually stretch all the way to the Dreaming Sea? If it does, it would be larger than the entire Scavenger Lands and around 2/3rds as large as the Realm is. In fact, it would be staggeringly large compared to virtually all of the other named states in Exalted. Granted if it were that big it would make sense it could be in some kind of conflict with Ysyr, but from the write up and the map I definitely never got the feeling that Prasad was intended to be that massive.<br /> <br /> The capital of Prasad is about as far from the Dreaming Sea as Gem is from the Inland Sea. If Prasad is supposed to be that massive, an empire second only in size to the Realm, then it seems like a shame that that didn't come through in it's writeup at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-21-2017, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:11:37-08:00","id":1052918,"title":"","content":"This has been a super interesting and illuminating thread. I feel like I know more about both the setting and the real world now. Thank you for everybody that has participated. I think I understand the Dreaming Sea a bit better now, in particular the Imperial Power bit from Eric above (and the links Isator posted) were helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:21:10-08:00","id":1052925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052912#post1052912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So like, does Prasad actually stretch all the way to the Dreaming Sea? If it does, it would be larger than the entire Scavenger Lands and around 2/3rds as large as the Realm is. In fact, it would be staggeringly large compared to virtually all of the other named states in Exalted. Granted if it were that big it would make sense it could be in some kind of conflict with Ysyr, but from the write up and the map I definitely never got the feeling that Prasad was intended to be that massive.<br /> <br /> The capital of Prasad is about as far from the Dreaming Sea as Gem is from the Inland Sea. If Prasad is supposed to be that massive, an empire second only in size to the Realm, then it seems like a shame that that didn't come through in it's writeup at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original writeup for Champoor indicated that it was a Prasadi client state. While it's possible that the devs cut this for setting reasons, I am under the impression that it was merely cut for space.<br /> <br /> Note that &quot;2/3 as large as the Realm&quot; presumes that the Realm's area is limited to the Blessed Isle, which is not the case. In any event, establishing two points on the map is insufficient to determine land area; Kamthahar could be at the center of a vast sprawl of Prasadi territory extending out in all directions, or it could at the western edge of Prasadi territory, with much of that territory existing in a narrow band along the banks of a river connecting it to the Dreaming Sea. The truth is doubtless somewhere in between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:26:04-08:00","id":1052928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052912#post1052912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So like, does Prasad actually stretch all the way to the Dreaming Sea? If it does, it would be larger than the entire Scavenger Lands and around 2/3rds as large as the Realm is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though you're presuming that Prasad would need to have territory spreading out more or less as a circle out from the capital.<br /> <br /> \u200bConsider the possibility that Prasad would have territory that reaches the Dreaming Sea, except that it's <i>really</i> narrow.<br /> <br /> \u200bPersonally, I don't assume that Prasad stretches to the Dreaming Sea; just to the edge of what is stretching out from Ysyr.<br /> <br /> \u200bPossibly, it has &quot;alliances&quot; (which are a bit more like vassalage) with some states in between their territory and the shores of the sea.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, I presume that somewhere between that large mountain range and that big body of water, there are maybe some rivers.<br /> <br /> Maybe even some rivers that have been made by Prasad.<br /> <br /> \u200bConsider the fact that China has had a system of canals that stretches continuously for more than a thousand miles since the <i>6th century</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The capital of Prasad is about as far from the Dreaming Sea as Gem is from the Inland Sea.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGem which probably sends and receives regular caravans from the Inland Sea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:32:22-08:00","id":1052933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052925#post1052925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original writeup for Champoor indicated that it was a Prasadi client state. While it's possible that the devs cut this for setting reasons, I am under the impression that it was merely cut for space.<br /> <br /> Note that &quot;2/3 as large as the Realm&quot; presumes that the Realm's area is limited to the Blessed Isle, which is not the case. In any event, establishing two points on the map is insufficient to determine land area; Kamthahar could be at the center of a vast sprawl of Prasadi territory extending out in all directions, or it could at the western edge of Prasadi territory, with much of that territory existing in a narrow band along the banks of a river connecting it to the Dreaming Sea. The truth is doubtless somewhere in between.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish this had gotten explored better and material hadn't been cut. When I read about Prasad and saw Kamthahar's location on the map, the idea that it was a big power in the Dreaming Sea simply didn't occur to me. It would be like saying Icehome is one of the great powers of the Scavenger Lands. Too bad the map is already printed or I'd have suggested moving the capital about 1000 miles east. <br /> <br /> When I read about Ysyr and Prasad being in conflict, I got the idea that perhaps they both had diplomats in a third party kingdom somewhere in the middle and occasionally interacted with one another that way. I just didn't think that they could be engaged in any kind of direct and sustained confrontation considering the sheer distance between them was similar to that of Gem and Paragon.<br /> <br /> All good though, thanks for clearing up how Creation is supposed to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:41:21-08:00","id":1052936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052918#post1052918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I know more about both the setting and the real world now. Thank you for everybody that has participated. I think I understand the Dreaming Sea a bit better now, in particular the Imperial Power bit from Eric above (and the links Isator posted) were helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSee, I love reading about this kind of history, because it gives me a greater appreciation for the ingenuity and connectivity that humans have always had. I love reading about things like how the presence of cinnamon in ancient tombs means that there have been trade links that transported goods between the areas we now call Sri Lanka and Egypt for at least four thousand years. I love considering how actual history showing the connections across the length of Europe, Asia and Africa for millennia emphasizes how strange and new it was to contact the people living in the Americas, and makes me more impressed with the fact that these people separated by thousands of years were able to communicate in a sophisticated manner within what might have been less than a decade.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt emphasizes to me that, in all times and places, even if they didn't necessarily have the same scope of terminology and hardware, people as a whole have been fairly smart and often heavily motivated.<br /> <br /> It is uplifting, and humbling.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs it pertains to Exalted, well, Exalted is a big part of what taught me to look for these things in the world, and I want to play games of Exalted where these details are evident because I would feel that playing somebody who rises to the top of all of it and draws upon it and influences its direction would be very enriching.<br /> <br /> \u200bI suppose it's part of why my perspective on the penultimate failure state for Creation is one in which it all becomes terribly fragmented. That's not to say that I envision the win condition as being a matter of total planar unification, just that rather than a rich tapestry you've got a thousand dominions in constant competition with the strength of the Exalted behind that, until the world becomes exhausted and one force or another causes it to end with a whimper.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:53:30-08:00","id":1052941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052928#post1052928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bGem which probably sends and receives regular caravans from the Inland Sea.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between Gem sending a few caravans to the Inland Sea and the book stating that Gem is an important and major player in the events of the Inland Sea. That was how Gem was presented in 1st edition and there were... issues with that presentation.<br /> <br /> Prasad is apparently supposed to be fairly exceptional in the standards of Exalted. Even if its &quot;width&quot; was only a few miles across, if it does reach all the way to the Dreaming Sea, it would still be one of the largest empires in terms of land area that we've seen in the setting besides Halta back during 1st edition. Unfortunately until that exchange I just had with Eric, I had simply assumed that it Prasad and Ysyr engaging with one another was another &quot;oops,&quot; in the vein of other map to text mistakes Exalted has made (Gem/Paragon) over the years.<br /> <br /> So in that light, I think it's entirely understandable for people to read about Prasad, look on the map and say, &quot;That doesn't make sense.&quot; At least that's what I came away. Having had this exchange with Eric, it's cool that it <i>is</i> supposed to work that way, and that it <i>wasn't</i> a mistake on the part of the writers like Halta or Gem were, but now all I can do is feel a slight sense of frustration that this didn't come across in the book at all.<br /> <br /> Hopefully the size, shape and land area of Prasad are something that will get explored better in a future book because if Prasad is supposed to be that big (even if it's pretty narrow it would still stretch around 60% the length of the Blessed Isle which would easily make it one of the largest nations we've ever seen in the setting) it's probably worth spending some word count discussing that fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T18:49:55-08:00","id":1052965,"title":"","content":"I'm pleased to hear that folks are finding these posts to be useful. It's unfortunate that so much of the corebook's Threshold writeups got cut, but on the plus side, this offers a lot of slack to whoever gets assigned to flesh out the material in some future supplement.<br /> <br /> While writing up Kamthahar, I'd intended for it to be well to the north, somewhere around the Dreaming Sea's northwest terminus and the accompanying cluster of giant lakes (or, perhaps, small seas). I suspect that the preponderance of the empire's populace and wealth is to be found in that area, with Kamthahar itself an outlier and the steppes in between proving to be lightly populated. Kamthahar itself may not be the empire's original capital. But all that remains up in the air until a relevant supplement is outlined and written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T19:02:15-08:00","id":1052968,"title":"","content":"Looking back at the map, it occurs to me that it's very conceivable that Ysyr doesn't want to fight for control of territory that extends inland, but along coastlines.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, my initial thought was that Prasad might have territory that extends east from Kamthahar until it reaches either the shore or a lot of subordinate coastal kingdoms, and that Ysyr's mainland territory might actually share little border with them, but it's a border that is heavily contested because Ysyr would want to expand northwest towards the trade routes to the Scavenger Lands, but then I realised &quot;look at how much water is there, going in that same direction&quot;, and also remembered how much of the Portuguese empire consisted of coastal settlements so that their ships around the horn of Africa would have places to dock on their way to the Indian ocean, as well as the maritime empires of the Mediterranean.<br /> <br /> \u200bI still imagine that Ysyr owns some of the mainland, but could actually picture it as having expanded into that primarily for the sake of being able to maintain a second front of pressure in any wars against Prasad. I think that's supposed to be why the Carthaginians expanded into the Iberian peninsula during the First Punic War.<br /> <br /> \u200bIndeed, looking at the placement of what are supposed to be the big empires of the southeast, I think it would be very fun to imagine them as having significantly different and incompatible territorial goals.<br /> <br /> \u200bPrasad is largely a land-based empire; it expanded directly to the sea, just enough west to have a lock on any traffic passing through the mountains, and is able to concentrate a lot of power in the narrow northern tip of the sea while overall not being very maritime. It has a larger population, maintains a lot of power over surrounding client states, is able to collect a massive bulk of goods through its meagre ports and firm control of the overland routes to the northern markets. It's able to police the top of the sea to ensure that a lot of trade has to pass through it, and has enough of a cultural tie to the Realm to ensure a decent reception for its traders on the other side of Ma-Ha-Suchi's domain. Their primary goal is to maintain their current monopolies, and gradually increase their control over the grasslands between the Dreaming Sea and the mountains.<br /> <br /> \u200bVolivat doesn't have the landmass that its competitors do, but it has a large network of colonies along the edge of the Dreaming Sea, superior naval power, and its control of the northern side of the Dreaming Sea is largely uncontested. This confers the advantages of having access to a lot of trade goods that the southern empires don't have native access to, as well as allowing it to connect to trade routes that spread north, most notably ones that are able to most effectively bypass Ma-Ha-Suchi's domain. They don't have much need to expand, but know that many of their southern settlements are seen as encroaching on enemy territory, and have a desire to repulse Ysyr's ambitions to establish footholds on the north.<br /> <br /> \u200bYsyr is the most powerful force on the big island it resides on (which is where a lot of the subservient city-states it is connected to by roads are found, and which it does not have complete control over), and is the furthest away from the lucrative northern trading. It wants to expend its power north largely through establishing dominance over the coastlines of the entire Dreaming Sea, with land-based expansion largely for the sake of having a stronger strategic base for contesting its foes and establishing a bread basket to relieve the burden on its heavily mountainous island territory. Being by far the closest to the Wyld is a unique challenge and advantage for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I read about Ysyr and Prasad being in conflict, I got the idea that perhaps they both had diplomats in a third party kingdom somewhere in the middle and occasionally interacted with one another that way. I just didn't think that they could be engaged in any kind of direct and sustained confrontation considering the sheer distance between them</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI imagine that one day we may get a Different Skies book focusing on the region, which may elaborate some of the details of its territorial distributions, but in the meantime* I look at it in terms of being given details that are firm enough to give direction and scant enough to leave a lot to fill in, and thinking that the exact details can be filled in by the desires and sensibilities of the individual.<br /> <br /> Do Ysyr and Prasad share a direct border? Do they engage largely through subservient intermediaries? Are they mostly struggling over coastal possessions? Does Ysyr want to take over (territory from) Prasad, or is it the other way around? Are they, in fact, in competition over expansion to seize control of the northern coastlines of the Dreaming Sea, with Volivat as their main native target which pursues a strategy of alternatively fighting them both off, allying with one against the other, and keeping them engaged with one another so that they're off balance?<br /> <br /> \u200bAdjust to taste.<br /> <br /> \u200b* I mean, even if we ever get a book like that, there would be nothing preventing me or anybody else from reassigning their possessions or ambitions or conflicts if something different suited any given game, or simply for the variety.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T19:04:26-08:00","id":1052970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052965#post1052965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pleased to hear that folks are finding these posts to be useful. It's unfortunate that so much of the corebook's Threshold writeups got cut, but on the plus side, this offers a lot of slack to whoever gets assigned to flesh out the material in some future supplement.<br /> <br /> While writing up Kamthahar, I'd intended for it to be well to the north, somewhere around the Dreaming Sea's northwest terminus and the accompanying cluster of giant lakes (or, perhaps, small seas). I suspect that the preponderance of the empire's populace and wealth is to be found in that area, with Kamthahar itself an outlier and the steppes in between proving to be lightly populated. Kamthahar itself may not be the empire's original capital. But all that remains up in the air until a relevant supplement is outlined and written.</div> </div> </div> </div>*takes notes*<br /> <br /> Kamthahar... in... wrong... place...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Don't mind me, this is much more useful than my original thread's premise. I'mma just keep an eye on this 'cuz it's super helpful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T19:09:38-08:00","id":1052974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052965#post1052965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While writing up Kamthahar, I'd intended for it to be well to the north, somewhere around the Dreaming Sea's northwest terminus and the accompanying cluster of giant lakes (or, perhaps, small seas). I suspect that the preponderance of the empire's populace and wealth is to be found in that area, with Kamthahar itself an outlier and the steppes in between proving to be lightly populated. Kamthahar itself may not be the empire's original capital. But all that remains up in the air until a relevant supplement is outlined and written.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could write it as Kamthahar being a relatively new capital. Prasad had an older capital closer to the Dreaming Sea and just &quot;recently&quot; (within the last century or so) made Kamthahar their capital, a bit reminiscent of Kyoto and Edo. Of course, then that begs the question as to why they would move their capital away from the Dreaming Sea out into, essentially, the middle of nowhere in the first place. Perhaps a prophecy? Maybe the ruler had a dream? Maybe the old capital was hit by a plague or other disaster?<br /> <br /> I don't think Kamthahar's location is the sort of thing that <i>needs</i> justification, but there are probably a lot of interesting ideas you could come up with for why it's located where it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T19:16:39-08:00","id":1052977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052970#post1052970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *takes notes*<br /> <br /> Kamthahar... in... wrong... place...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Don't mind me, this is much more useful than my original thread's premise. I'mma just keep an eye on this 'cuz it's super helpful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>... It would never have occurred to me to invoke Neighborhood Relocation Scheme in this context.<br /> <br /> I feel confident that this will not be the canon explanation for Kamthahar's location. But if it works for you in your game, please let me know how your players react when they find out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T19:17:35-08:00","id":1052978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052977#post1052977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... It would never have occurred to me to invoke Neighborhood Relocation Scheme in this context.<br /> <br /> I feel confident that this will not be the canon explanation for Kamthahar's location. But if it works for you in your game, please let me know how your players react when they find out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly referring to it being a map error, but hell, I probably need more Sidereal plots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T19:24:40-08:00","id":1052983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052978#post1052978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was mostly referring to it being a map error, but hell, I probably need more Sidereal plots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if &quot;map error&quot; is strictly accurate. I put together a now-lost rough sketch of the Threshold and passed it on to the developers, who then conveyed information to the cartographer. I can no longer recall whether I accidentally placed Kamthahar on that sketch in an unintended location, or if the devs decided that they specifically wanted it moved, or if the cartographer simply decided it looked better there.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I'd also intended for the Haslanti cities to be closer together; ditto for Rubylak and Chanta. In those cases, too, I may well be as responsible for their spread-out placement as anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T19:28:09-08:00","id":1052987,"title":"","content":"Regardless of anything else, Exalted 3rd edition's map is honestly one of the absolutely best looking fantasy maps I've ever seen. And I've seen a bunch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T19:35:49-08:00","id":1052990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052974#post1052974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, then that raises the question as to why they would move their capital away from the Dreaming Sea out into, essentially, the middle of nowhere in the first place. Perhaps a prophecy? Maybe the ruler had a dream? Maybe the old capital was hit by a plague or other disaster?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of the most straightforward reasons for a country to shift capitals is because the territory containing the prior capital was conquered.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's what happened with the Song Dynasty. From a certain perspective, it's what happened with the Roman empire.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd say it's a bit fitting for the tone established for the southeast.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy own current narrative for Kathahar's placement is that it was a Realm colony established in the safety of outlying regions of existing southeastern powers that extended its powers through them towards the Dreaming Sea. The original plan would have called for eventual relocation, but by the time Prasad became a major power the Exalted colonists had become entrenched in their new caste system and heretical offshoot that left them very attached to their original city.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T20:03:08-08:00","id":1053000,"title":"","content":"In my last game (the prequel to Jetstream's current game) I decided that the trade passage from Kamthahar down through the South was the only way for tribute to reliably flow back to the Realm. Good ole MHS makes anything else just too damned risky. I then set up a tricky political relationship between the Realm and three DB-ruled city-states along that route. It worked out pretty well overall.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I can imagine the route was also the original one blazed by the Dynasts who went to the Dreaming Sea. In that case, Kamthahar was founded due to local geography (mines, a lake, etc). It was not intended to be the capital of an empire. That just happened because Exalts will be Exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T20:23:00-08:00","id":1053011,"title":"","content":"Recalling the original question of the thread, I've now got an image in which the more public attitude of Ysyr regarding the Dragon Blooded of Prasad is that they are amongst the venerable and respectable Exalted who have been bestowed dominion over the Earth, while their basis for opposing them is partially rationalized to any buffer kingdoms and vassal cities that they're trying to flip with &quot;but you know, having them sitting on the doorstep of the relatively reasonable Anathema who is lying between us and the more convenient routes to the Inland Sea and Scavenger Lands makes things a lot more difficult for us than they have to be. I mean, good on them and all, fight the good fight, but maybe we could very firmly insist that they have their good fight from a direction that makes it easier for us to establish a deal with Ma-Ha-Suchi up until the time when they inevitably and properly kill him&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, add that to the priorities for Prasad's expansion; trying to establish territory that leaves Ma-Ha-Suchi's domain more thoroughly surrounded.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso add that to the conception of what it means for a lot of people to regard the Lunars (and Solars) as Anathema; friendly relations might occasionally be desired, but parsed in a lot of equivocation around whether you would really stoop to consorting with such monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T21:48:31-08:00","id":1053038,"title":"","content":"Okay, this thread in general seems to be laboring under a couple of assumptions (Though I might be misreading or mistaken) that I'm not sure I agree with.<br /> <br /> 1: That most large nations have large enclaves of Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> 2: That the Immaculate Philosophy is a mainstream religion in regions outside of the Realm's direct control.<br /> <br /> Now, don't get me wrong, there are probably scads of lone DBs and some sworn brotherhoods here and there, but I think any nation that has a bunch of Dragon-Blooded is, by default, a big deal. The Realm is the largest and most obvious, while Lookshy and Prasad are noteworthy, but I feel that most nations are ruled by humans, Sorcerers, God-Blooded and the like, especially if the nation's write-up doesn't mention having a large contingent of Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> As Far as the Immaculate Philosophy goes, I imagine that only Satrapies and client states of the Realm actually follow it, with some altered versions like Prasad's Pure Way here and there. Outside of Realm-dominated ares, I feel that worship of local Gods, Elementals, Fair-Folk and so forth tends to dominate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T23:59:39-08:00","id":1053075,"title":"","content":"So I dug around in the leak book with the assumption that write-up cuts were due to word count rather than changes to the setting. This <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> extracted from Prasad\u2019s client states around the western Dreaming Sea </div> </div> </div> talks about how Prasad pays its tribute to the realm. So its influence and control reaches the Dreaming Seas. Champoor is also mentioned as a client state of Prasad. <br /> <br /> For Ysyr Palanquin is said to have been conquered by them a century ago.<br /> <br /> So I have drawn up a rough example of how I view these empires in terms of their control of the territory around them. In this way the distance between their borders, between where they have strong control, is only around 1200 miles. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s1.postimg.org/pxuocse6n/YSyr_og_Prasad.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4567-volivat","name":"Volivat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T00:57:09-08:00","id":1053092,"title":"","content":"I would imagine that Ysyr has less penetration onto the mainland and that it would be focused around Palanquin, likewise for Kamthahar and the coast near Champoor. These are helpful for trying to imagine these, though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T02:38:34-08:00","id":1053108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052527#post1052527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI'm going to assume that &quot;sources of Terrestrial bloodlines&quot; is referring to places where Exaltation might be disproportionately common.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was also thinking of places where Dragon-Blooded ancestry is culturally significant but not reflected by current exaltation rates. Something like the Cynis Denovah family if they were based outside of the Realm rather than a lesser branch of a Great House.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T02:50:04-08:00","id":1053110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052974#post1052974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could write it as Kamthahar being a relatively new capital. Prasad had an older capital closer to the Dreaming Sea and just &quot;recently&quot; (within the last century or so) made Kamthahar their capital, a bit reminiscent of Kyoto and Edo. Of course, then that begs the question as to why they would move their capital away from the Dreaming Sea out into, essentially, the middle of nowhere in the first place. Perhaps a prophecy? Maybe the ruler had a dream? Maybe the old capital was hit by a plague or other disaster?</div> </div> </div> </div>One idea: from what I know, in real life history there's been a competing pressure - capital cities serve as military and economic hubs. <br /> <br /> From many of the capital cities of China initially were not always best placed for an economic hub for the country, or for sea trade access. They were often placed where the military faced off against the boundaries of Inner Asia that Chinese civilization had difficulty expanding into (poorly suited for agriculture). <br /> <br /> In those places people tended to build the most military capacity, and therefore the dynasties that took over China tended to come to power from there, and tended to keep a military power base there. <br /> <br /> Then it usually goes to shift towards Beijing as the compromise (ideal position for access to the sea and China against good position for a military capital positioned vs the steppes, then reinforced repeatedly by history). <br /> <br /> (Some have said the Grand Principality of Moscow is another similar example - geographically peripheral, but with the right conditions to catalyze a military dominance.)<br /> <br /> (Above based on pretty limited knowledge, so happy to be corrected if wrong).<br /> <br /> Kamthahar's position on the map actually necessarily doesn't look like such a bad fit for that model, on the borders of land fertile enough that a Blessed Isle like civilization could hold and a place where it might have more difficulty, though I think it seems a bit extremely positioned even still. <br /> <br /> (This said, I don't know that it necessarily fits with the Dreaming Sea as a whole, if it is like the classical Mediterranean and all the locus of military competition where the big expansionist powers, er... &quot;nucleate&quot; was along the Mediterranean Sea.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T03:58:32-08:00","id":1053124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zealot_Vedas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1053038#post1053038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Far as the Immaculate Philosophy goes, I imagine that only Satrapies and client states of the Realm actually follow it, with some altered versions like Prasad's Pure Way here and there. Outside of Realm-dominated ares, I feel that worship of local Gods, Elementals, Fair-Folk and so forth tends to dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI would be inclined to come up with some religions that go a bit beyond simply worshipping gods.<br /> <br /> At least have some narratives that perpetuate a strong and cohesive sense of why any given god should be worshipped above others.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:10:50-08:00","id":1053176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volivat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1053075#post1053075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So I dug around in the leak book with the assumption that write-up cuts were due to word count rather than changes to the setting. This talks about how Prasad pays its tribute to the realm. So its influence and control reaches the Dreaming Seas. Champoor is also mentioned as a client state of Prasad.<br /> <br /> For Ysyr Palanquin is said to have been conquered by them a century ago.<br /> <br /> So I have drawn up a rough example of how I view these empires in terms of their control of the territory around them. In this way the distance between their borders, between where they have strong control, is only around 1200 miles.<br /> <br /> &lt;snip image&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice work on that. This raises a couple questions:<br /> 1. What are Volivat's borders like? If I wanted to make things especially tense, I'd say Ydanna is their client state. I searched the core book and the leak and found nothing on it.<br /> 2. Just how many competing minor kingdoms and city-states are between the two of them. I could easily see expanding their borders towards each other, but it might be more fun to throw an extra large Hundred Kingdoms-style region in there. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:38:53-08:00","id":1053235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1053176#post1053176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice work on that. This raises a couple questions:<br /> 1. What are Volivat's borders like? If I wanted to make things especially tense, I'd say Ydanna is their client state. I searched the core book and the leak and found nothing on it.<br /> 2. Just how many competing minor kingdoms and city-states are between the two of them. I could easily see expanding their borders towards each other, but it might be more fun to throw an extra large Hundred Kingdoms-style region in there. </div> </div> </div> </div>... ... ...<br /> <br /> *more notes*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T12:44:59-08:00","id":1053375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1053176#post1053176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice work on that. This raises a couple questions:<br /> 1. What are Volivat's borders like? If I wanted to make things especially tense, I'd say Ydanna is their client state. I searched the core book and the leak and found nothing on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't go into any detail about Y'danna, but based on its original writeup from the developers, it is not a political player in the Dreaming Sea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1053176#post1053176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Just how many competing minor kingdoms and city-states are between the two of them. I could easily see expanding their borders towards each other, but it might be more fun to throw an extra large Hundred Kingdoms-style region in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are definitely a great number of minor principalities, city-states, peoples and tribes along the shores of the Dreaming Sea. How many are independent of the extant imperial powers, I can't say. But as the region was intended to allow for the addition of lesser powers with imperial ambition, it is best to assume that the borders of the great powers are fragmented and that at any given time there are populations under no one's direct military or political control. This may be due to negotiated neutrality; treaty-based devassalization; ongoing or successful rebellion; or <i>de facto</i> independence due to the withdrawal of overstretched occupying forces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:51:28-08:00","id":1053431,"title":"","content":"It's funny; the southeast already invokes some of the history of India, with its numerous kingdoms that go back and forth between being part of empires, its wealth, its measure of isolation, and some of the terminology used in the core.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut then I considered how, in terms of its geographic layout, it even resembles a kind of inversion of the subcontinent; triangular water with land on both sides of it.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs a personal example of reaching, I could even see a little parallel between the dangers of the Dreaming Sea and the taboos that Hinduism has about travelling on the open ocean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:41:14-08:00","id":1053503,"title":"","content":"On a total tangent triggered in my mind on Levi's post: On the aesthetics and feel of the &quot;great powers&quot;, I find Prasad brings to mind India. Volivat I find harder to place. <br /> <br /> While Ys brings to mind, well... Ys, the island of legend.. so I guess so at least in part evokes Jack Vance's Lyonesse, and that whole fusion of decadent, doomed Sword and Sorcery sensibilities with Arthurian, Celtic and the European High Middle Ages, somehow sitting along with the more psychadelic feel of the Dreaming Sea. This, is a reference I'm almost certain the authors do not intend to be descriptive- because of the general dynamics of the Southeast in particular, and Creation in general - but, there's that name (which just feels like it surely has to somehow be a reference to the Ys of myth?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T18:42:02-08:00","id":1053567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1053124#post1053124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI would be inclined to come up with some religions that go a bit beyond simply worshipping gods.<br /> <br /> At least have some narratives that perpetuate a strong and cohesive sense of why any given god should be worshipped above others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah that makes sense. Also, I completely forgot about ancestor worship. I was just giving those as examples of &quot;the Immaculate Faith isn't everywhere&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T18:49:48-08:00","id":1053569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1053503#post1053503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a total tangent triggered in my mind on Levi's post: On the aesthetics and feel of the &quot;great powers&quot;, I find Prasad brings to mind India. Volivat I find harder to place.<br /> <br /> While Ys brings to mind, well... Ys, the island of legend.. so I guess so at least in part evokes Jack Vance's Lyonesse, and that whole fusion of decadent, doomed Sword and Sorcery sensibilities with Arthurian, Celtic and the European High Middle Ages, somehow sitting along with the more psychadelic feel of the Dreaming Sea. This, is a reference I'm almost certain the authors do not intend to be descriptive- because of the general dynamics of the Southeast in particular, and Creation in general - but, there's that name (which just feels like it surely has to somehow be a reference to the Ys of myth?).</div> </div> </div> </div>The developers came up with the name &quot;Ysyr,&quot; and I am not privy to their thought processes in the matter. But I added the term &quot;Ys&quot; for the corebook writeup, and I definitely had both the mythical Ys and Jack Vance's Lyonesse in mind when I did so. This shouldn't be taken to indicate the presence of medieval Western European cultural markers, though the decadent, doomed Sword &amp; Sorcery sensibilities should be there in spades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T19:02:22-08:00","id":1053573,"title":"","content":"Oh, and also the Ys from John Brunner's <i>The Traveller in Black</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T19:39:55-08:00","id":1053589,"title":"","content":"Ysyr always made me think of Assyrian (Yssyrian sounds very similair), so I model their aesthetics on the Assyrian Empire.<br /> Volviat ...I don't know, I made them Levant-Cannanite/Vaugely Israeli? I think the ten fathers immediately connected to ten tribes in my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T20:28:28-08:00","id":1053608,"title":"","content":"Something about the statement of Prasad potentially being a third the size of the Realm made me think of some historical comparisons.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor one thing, I frequently have to remind myself that if the Blessed Isle existed on Earth, it would be the second biggest country, not much smaller than Russia, relatively speaking. If the imperial territory of the Realm consisted solely of the Isle, that would already qualify it as something like the fourth or fifth biggest empire in history.<br /> <br /> \u200bThen you consider its holdings in the Threshold; I mean, they're not directly administered or colonised by the Realm, but they still belong to its territory, so considering exactly how much land one considers that to constitute, the Realm could be almost as large as the Mongol, or even British empire.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf I measure it in terms of land area, the Roman empire was about a third the size of modern day Russia. That does sound like a lot, but if I just look at a map of Eurasia and compare the placement of the two, Russia still really looks like it absolutely dwarfs the Romans, even if one includes the actual area of the Mediterranean sea.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven without just looking at it on a map, to consider the scope and breadth of Russia (whether the modern form or its largest historical empire); the extent of its diversity of peoples, of landscapes, or climate zones; maybe it's just me, but Russia feels like it's a lot more than the mathematical comparison between other empires.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf I consider Prasad to be roughly the size and shape of the Achaemenid empire, then it still looks and feels as though it's a lot smaller than the Realm, even if it is vastly greater than any state that has to try growing within reach of the Realm's legions could ever be.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for the assertion that its capital is in the middle of nowhere, we're back to the idea that only the things shown on this zoomed out map are important, as well as a bit of the typical Western thing of assuming that the big body of water is 100% defining. The amount of land in between the Dreaming Sea and the Summer mountains that the map colours in green is about the size of Russia; I presume it has to have a number of important cities strewn around in there, many of which are hundreds of kilometres away from the Dreaming Sea. Certainly, I assume that it has to have at least a few cities that are more important than Champoor. When I'm introduced to the capital of what is supposed to be one of the big empires in the region, I think my first thought should not be &quot;why is it in the middle of nowhere&quot;, but rather &quot;what interesting things are there that helps it to be so important&quot;.<br /> <br /> Totentanz has already pointed out that it's fairly well placed to access trade to and from the west.<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, it's a fair distance away from the Dreaming Sea. It's about the same distance as Delhi is from its closest shore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T08:21:10-08:00","id":1053828,"title":"","content":"When drawing comparisons between Prasad, the Realm, and real-world empires, we should also consider other factors. Russia is huge, yes. A large chunk of that territory is semi-useless. The Realm, on the other hand, sits on the Blessed Isle, the most fertile and climatically stable area of Creation. It has the best geomantic resources, the most existing infrastructure, and of course its rulers possess the lion's share of the treasure from the past Age. None of that factors in its Threshold possessions, which the Empress has optimized for feeding her empire money and manpower for her armies. I'm not sure our world has ever seen an empire as dominant as the Realm.<br /> <br /> Of course, Ex3 takes a hands-off approach to world-building, so individual groups can throw in competing power centers as they see fit.<br /> <br /> It's hard to make a direct comparison on these fronts between the Realm and Prasad, because we don't know nearly as much about the Dreaming Sea region as a whole, unfortunately. If we assume the standard elemental associations apply, Prasad will be more stable and cooler, but less fecund than Ysyr.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T08:41:07-08:00","id":1053837,"title":"","content":"Tossing in another picture to help get a clear picture of the size of the dreaming seas...<br /> <br /> Each damned square there is in terms of size equivalent to 1.2 modern day France... So There should be numerous large cities/empires/kingdoms in the dreaming seas. Not to mention the countless hamlets, villages and small towns.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i65.tinypic.com/11l26ja.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4567-volivat","name":"Volivat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T16:30:23-08:00","id":1054075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1052460#post1052460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's very much the tone that was set by Exalted: The Outcastes where rather than focusing on attitudes and potential sources of Terrestrial Bloodlines it kind of assumes everywhere has a thriving Dragon-Blooded community unless it got poached by the Realm or wiped out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem is that it frequently tries to communicate the potential of Outcaste Dragon-Blooded through stereotype rather than example.<br /> If (for example) you say that Outcaste women in Chiaroscuro tend to take the grey some people are going to read that as them being common enough to draw trends when the author may actually be trying to say that the life of a male Delzhan has more uses for the kind of power Dragon-Blooded wield.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T05:14:13-08:00","id":1057539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1053573#post1053573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and also the Ys from John Brunner's <i>The Traveller in Black</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Say... you might KNOW this...<br /> <br /> On the map, Ysyr (and other locales) are in special little circles. Are those circles like... &quot;magnifying glasses,&quot; blowing up smaller territory to show us its topography? Or is Ysyr really that huge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T08:43:55-08:00","id":1057610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1057539#post1057539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the map, Ysyr (and other locales) are in special little circles. Are those circles like... &quot;magnifying glasses,&quot; blowing up smaller territory to show us its topography? Or is Ysyr really that huge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah; that was not clear at all. Gloam, Bluehaven, and Sunken Luthe do rather look to be magnifying an important feature in a tiny dot in the ocean, don't they?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, in EX2 Onyx was about the same size as Azure and Abalone (the other two biggest islands of the Coral and Wavecrest Archapelegos), and Bluehaven was positioned where the city icon is in EX3, rather than the dot. I also believe that the Caul is supposed to be to scale with the rest of the map. Thus I'd say the circles are just highlights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T12:29:52-08:00","id":1057717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1057539#post1057539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Say... you might KNOW this...<br /> <br /> On the map, Ysyr (and other locales) are in special little circles. Are those circles like... &quot;magnifying glasses,&quot; blowing up smaller territory to show us its topography? Or is Ysyr really that huge?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have access to special knowledge about this, but Bluehaven, Gloam, Onyx, and Sunken Luthe all share the same sort of &quot;zoomed-in&quot; circles that suggest that they are not to scale. Ysyr's circle doesn't have that same look, which suggests that the island is to scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T13:01:11-08:00","id":1057727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1057717#post1057717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have access to special knowledge about this, but Bluehaven, Gloam, Onyx, and Sunken Luthe all share the same sort of &quot;zoomed-in&quot; circles that suggest that they are not to scale. Ysyr's circle doesn't have that same look, which suggests that the island is to scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>... We really could use a map key. Like badly. There are a ton of flourishes on the map that could be aesthetic, or they could be signaling something, but it's completely unclear as to what. And those circles, if they mean <b>different things,</b> are super misleading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T13:36:35-08:00","id":1057746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1057717#post1057717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have access to special knowledge about this, but Bluehaven, Gloam, Onyx, and Sunken Luthe all share the same sort of &quot;zoomed-in&quot; circles that suggest that they are not to scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe Skullstone Archipelago seems to be an odd addition to those considering that it's a bunch of islands rather than city, and considering how Wu Jian is drawn, it feels odd to single out one important island group for such and not another.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for the cities, are we saying that all of the other ones that don't have circles <i>are</i> to scale? That Gloam is a city the size of a city, i.e. something that would not actually be visible on a map at this scale, but that Nexus and Lookshy and Kirighast are the size of small countries?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:07:15-08:00","id":1057802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1057746#post1057746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Skullstone Archipelago seems to be an odd addition to those considering that it's a bunch of islands rather than city, and considering how Wu Jian is drawn, it feels odd to single out one important island group for such and not another.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be an error on the part of the cartographer. I can't say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1057746#post1057746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAs for the cities, are we saying that all of the other ones that don't have circles <i>are</i> to scale? That Gloam is a city the size of a city, i.e. something that would not actually be visible on a map at this scale, but that Nexus and Lookshy and Kirighast are the size of small countries?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the point is that Gloam is located on a relatively small island, one that would normally not be large enough to appear on the map at its current scale. Mind you, I'm not sure that Wu Jian's island should be large enough for that. The map should not generally be treated as a thing possessed of great in-setting precision.<br /> <br /> Your suggestion that the map scaling is for cities rather than for land masses is very silly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T18:28:27-08:00","id":1057861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1057802#post1057802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your suggestion that the map scaling is for cities rather than for land masses is very silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhh I'm very frustrated now. Part of that is that I've had a terrible week, buuuut...<br /> <br /> Okay, this line:<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the cities, are we saying that all of the other ones that don't have circles <i>are</i> to scale?\u200b </div> </div> </div>Is not me making a suggestion, or asking for confirmation of a fact.<br /> <br /> That line is me making a point that I find the suggestion that the circles represent magnification to not be consistent with other parts of the map.<br /> <br /> Indeed, this line:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> something that would not actually be visible on a map at this scale </div> </div> </div>\u200bIs me <i>directly stating</i> that neither this, nor any other map of a world, would be scaled to the size of cities.<br /> <br /> \u200bI apologise if this post is a bit salty; like I said, terrible week. Just the worst.<br /> <br /> \u200bI am also a bit touchy on occasions where something I've written is misread in a manner that I feel would make me come off as... very different.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T18:51:08-08:00","id":1057868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1057861#post1057861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ohhh I'm very frustrated now. Part of that is that I've had a terrible week, buuuut...</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies; I didn't mean to distress you. I was a bit salty myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":1120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","user":"Eric Minton","date":". 03-03-2017, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T19:58:21-08:00","id":1057900,"title":"","content":"Terrible week all around, it seems.<br /> <br /> Did <i>anyone</i> have a good week this week?<br /> <br /> Does anyone know if we can just mulligan this one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T21:22:26-08:00","id":1057923,"title":"","content":"Legit, my week sucked too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T07:01:08-08:00","id":1058023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1054075#post1054075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem is that it frequently tries to communicate the potential of Outcaste Dragon-Blooded through stereotype rather than example.<br /> If (for example) you say that Outcaste women in Chiaroscuro tend to take the grey some people are going to read that as them being common enough to draw trends when the author may actually be trying to say that the life of a male Delzhan has more uses for the kind of power Dragon-Blooded wield.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of this problem is the notion that every map dot has its own Dragon-Blooded unless its culture is actively pushing them out.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Exaltation has the potential to Exalt someone out of nowhere without any apparent Dragon-Blooded heritage but to me that was always something intended for player characters rather than a phenomena we should expect to see happening all over the world.<br /> <br /> IMO we should ask why a locale has Dragon-Blooded rather than why not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T09:36:03-08:00","id":1058063,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... while I prefer to have small Dragonblood dynasties in different areas (not necessarily that the whole family is Dragonblood, but a few members are... generally it'll be the royal family of course, but it could vary), because I think it's a)likely, and b)more interesting for both me and the players; I actually think it's a bit exaggerated to say that it's just a line to explain PCs. I think it actually is indeed intended that there are just random DBs in random places. There are about 10000 of them outside the Realm after all (of which Lookshy is just, I think, about 1000), which is a lot. Not a lot per country sure, but still.<br /> <br /> In fact, one of the reasons I like to put DB Outcastes into little families is that I think the books actually present the vast majority of those 10000 outcastes as being random guys with a Dragonblooded great-grandfather.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T09:49:06-08:00","id":1058069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058063#post1058063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, one of the reasons I like to put DB Outcastes into little families is that I think the books actually present the vast majority of those 10000 outcastes as being random guys with a Dragonblooded great-grandfather.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like that aspect, that actual families and dynasties of Dragon Blooded are fairly rare, and in the Threshold most Dragon Blooded simply Exalt on their own without any immediate relationship to any other Exalt. <br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, why don't you care for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T14:45:43-08:00","id":1058157,"title":"","content":"I can mostly speak of 2e because that's the edition that introduced me to Exalted.<br /> <br /> MoEP: Dragon-Blooded paints a picture of a world were random Outcastes seem to pop up so much that multiple places on the map are treating them like some contemptible mutant minority - Halta executing Fire Aspects because they might hurt the trees, Varang basically wanting all Exalts to fuck off because of their caste system, Coral being such devoted cock worshipers that they're encouraging female Outcastes to leave and the Bull of the North has got people hunting down and murdering Outcaste children like he's fucking Hitler.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T15:28:55-08:00","id":1058173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058069#post1058069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually like that aspect, that actual families and dynasties of Dragon Blooded are fairly rare, and in the Threshold most Dragon Blooded simply Exalt on their own without any immediate relationship to any other Exalt.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, why don't you care for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't detest it. I'm not horrified by random Outcastes everywhere. It's just that a)it's a bit dull, and b)since Dragonblood exaltation is passed by the blood, I'd expect various small families of Dragonblood, rather than just random dudes all over the place. It would seem kind of odd if the only DB families in the world are the Scarlet Dynasty, House Ferem, Lookshy's DBs, and... that's it (Were the Forest Witches related to each other?)<br /> <br /> I'd expect some random Outcastes, of course, but not just them. I mean, an Outcaste is more likely to have mortal kids than Dragonblood, but she's still far, far more likely to have Dragonblood kids than most people are.<br /> <br /> Also, it helps reinforce that Outcastes are not just lower-powered Solar-equivalent random heroes, but have their own thing going on. Family is a theme of Dragonblood, and Outcaste families let you explore it in other ways to the decadent royal Scarlet Dynasty.<br /> <br /> For example, perhaps a royal family with 1 Dragonblood every generation or two, or a Dragonblooded hero with 20 grandkids, one of whom is also a Dragonblood and is learning kung-fu from his grandpa.<br /> <br /> Also, I like to have bits and bobs from the Shogunate (because I always feel that, considering that it precedes the Second Age, the Shogunate is often overlooked by the fluff), so I've thrown in the occasional royal family that is descended from a Shogunate Daimyo, and has a few Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, in my recently-ended 3rd ed game, there were two non-Realm groups of DBs that the PCs encountered.<br /> <br /> The first, were the high priests/commanders of a country called Varamaya (but they weren't actually the government). The country had 5 elemental castes (wood-farmers, fire-soldiers, water-traders, etc), and each caste had DB priests at the top. Of course, the number of DBs in the country, while higher than neighbouring countries, was pretty small. There were 2 fire aspected cousins, an old earth aspect and his earth aspected grandson, 2 air aspects who were secretly half-siblings (because they were desperate not to let the bloodline die out), 3 water aspects two of which had had an arranged marriage, and 5 wood aspects in a group marriage. <br /> <br /> Another group I had was 4 similar countries each ruled by a Dragonblood King+Queen. Except actually most of the monarchs were only Dragonblood according to legal fiction; there was a total of one Dragonblood queen, one Dragonblood uncle-of-the-king, one elemental-blood-pretending-to-be-Dragonblood, and one undersea mutant pretending to be a Water aspect.<br /> <br /> So, I was playing the themes of family and decreasing blood purity that are part of Dragonblood.<br /> It seemed a lot more interesting than just having random Outcastes, as besides the family angle, it provided the Dragonblood with a place in the (local) setting and institutions, which I think is something that'd crop up a lot when you have mighty heroes who live for 300 years and in that time might well produce an heir with similar powers (and 30-odd kids without the powers, but who cares about them).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T15:43:38-08:00","id":1058178,"title":"","content":"This week was unfortunate, but it redeemed itself a bit with the fact that, against all probability, I actually moved up on the waiting list for a Nintendo Switch and was able to get one today, rather than a few weeks from now, despite having only placed an order the day before it was released.<br /> <br /> Anyway:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, perhaps a royal family with 1 Dragonblood every generation or two, or a Dragonblooded hero with 20 grandkids, one of whom is also a Dragonblood and is learning kung-fu from his grandpa.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's interesting how differences in terminology work out. What you're describing there is about the kind of thing I would expect and depict as well, and would not describe as being a Dragon Blooded family in most circumstances.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn the Realm they get called minor Houses, but they have the benefit of existing in the margins of families that more consistently produce Exalted.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T18:58:19-08:00","id":1058247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058173#post1058173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, perhaps a royal family with 1 Dragonblood every generation or two, or a Dragonblooded hero with 20 grandkids, one of whom is also a Dragonblood and is learning kung-fu from his grandpa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. This is an <i>excellent </i>way to arrange for an outcaste to have a mentor.* Of course, the imagery may suffer a bit when you recall that <i>grandpa </i>likely still <i>looks</i> to be in his twenties. However that's the very thing that forges closer ties among the few family members that do exalt.<br /> <br /> (* Heck, or for a solar too. &quot;She takes after her grandma so much, so what if she's glowing gold? Sigh.&quot;)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058173#post1058173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I like to have bits and bobs from the Shogunate (because I always feel that, considering that it precedes the Second Age, the Shogunate is often overlooked by the fluff), so I've thrown in the occasional royal family that is descended from a Shogunate Daimyo, and has a few Dragonblood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely overlooked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058173#post1058173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another group I had was 4 similar countries each ruled by a Dragonblood King+Queen. Except actually most of the monarchs were only Dragonblood according to legal fiction; there was a total of one Dragonblood queen, one Dragonblood uncle-of-the-king, one elemental-blood-pretending-to-be-Dragonblood, and one undersea mutant pretending to be a Water aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey. Sounds fun. I can see plenty of potential plot hooks forming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058173#post1058173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seemed a lot more interesting than just having random Outcastes, as besides the family angle, it provided the Dragonblood with a place in the (local) setting and institutions, which I think is something that'd crop up a lot when you have mighty heroes who live for 300 years and in that time might well produce an heir with similar powers (and 30-odd kids without the powers, but who cares about them).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they are still family, but there will be some distancing as they get older and you don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 03-04-2017, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T22:01:49-08:00","id":1058295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058157#post1058157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the Bull of the North has got people hunting down and murdering Outcaste children like he's fucking Hitler.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where was this part? I don't remember writing it, and I can't find anything in a search of my original draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T22:31:48-08:00","id":1058297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058295#post1058295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where was this part? I don't remember writing it, and I can't find anything in a search of my original draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your original draft of Manual of Exalted Power: Dragon Blooded? I didn't know you worked on that book.<br /> <br /> It's on page 61, btw, &quot;The icewalkers allied under Yurgen Kaneko, the Solar Exalted known as the Bull of the North, allow Terrestrials born of their tribes to remain as part of the growing warband. Those born in the small villages that dot his lands, however, are slain whenever the Bull's patrols discover them. As such, when Northern villagers in the Bull's path discover that one of their own has taken the Second Breath, that one is quickly sent into exile...&quot; it goes on to describe where they're sent yadda yadda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T22:39:14-08:00","id":1058300,"title":"","content":"Eh not really hunting down and murdering children then. I mean still not exactly a good thing, but from how Lioness phrased it I thought it was something like &quot;That one flared. Slaughter their family, every DB in the north dies.&quot; <br /> <br /> Which I also just couldn't get as I couldn't imagine someone turning down DBs as soldiers unless you suspected them of being infiltrators or something.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T22:42:18-08:00","id":1058301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058297#post1058297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your original draft of Manual of Exalted Power: Dragon Blooded? I didn't know you worked on that book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I wrote the section on the Bull of the North for <b>Compass of Terrestrial Directions: the North</b>. I blanked out for a moment on the fact that of course the Bull was referenced at earlier points in the second edition line,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T23:36:06-08:00","id":1058310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058300#post1058300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh not really hunting down and murdering children then. I mean still not exactly a good thing, but from how Lioness phrased it I thought it was something like &quot;That one flared. Slaughter their family, every DB in the north dies.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that's <i>exactly</i> what Dragon Blooded tend to say about Solars. Heck, the Wyld Hunt is even known to hurt, attack or hold a Solar's family as hostages in order to lure them out to be killed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058300#post1058300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which I also just couldn't get as I couldn't imagine someone turning down DBs as soldiers unless you suspected them of being infiltrators or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see it. At least as per 2nd edition, Yurgen Exalted before the Jade Prison broke. His Exaltation is one of the others that spent the last 1000+ years constantly being born and then quickly murdered by Dragon Blooded. Considering he probably has plenty of memories from his dozens of incarnations being killed over and over by Terrestrials, I never found it terribly surprising that he felt like returning the favor. Most Dragon Blooded give no quarter to Solars, so some Solars will give no quarter to Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> In a way the Solar/Dragon Blooded feud is a millennia old vendetta and those are almost always pretty brutal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-05-2017, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T01:03:56-08:00","id":1058318,"title":"","content":"I found it odd because in 1st ed he had a number of Outcaste lieutenants (including one who went into self-imposed exile when he realised the Bull wasn't really fighting to protect the North, but just for his own ambitions). Some of them used warstriders against the Realm.<br /> <br /> But then, I suppose that paragraph did say that they do allow Icewalker Outcastes, but not ones from the areas they've conquered. Which I guess is because he worries they'll grow up to fight for the freedom of their people.<br /> <br /> So, it's not so much a Solar vs Dragonblooded grudge, as wanting to keep the Icewalkers strong and the conquered areas thoroughly weak.<br /> <br /> Despite his few memories of fighting DBs, I think his 70 years of being an Icewalker is much more significant to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-05-2017, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T03:48:41-08:00","id":1058347,"title":"","content":"Also, the weight of the memories of his incarnations wouldn't necessarily give him this raging hate-on for DBs more than anyone else, seeing how Lytek is, y'know, doing his job and all. The Solars who've been reincarnating for the last thousand years aren't particularly likely to have more memories of past lives than any other Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T05:01:13-08:00","id":1058364,"title":"","content":"This really goes back to the problem I was talking about of Outcastes being talked about like they're common.<br /> <br /> I'll quote the full text.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP: Dragon-Blooded</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The icewalkers allied under Yurgen Kaneko, the Solar Exalt known as the Bull of the North, allow Terrestrials born of their tribes to remain as part of the growing warband. Those born in the small villages that dot his lands, however, are slain whenever the Bull\u2019s patrols discover them. As such, when Northern villagers in the Bull\u2019s path discover that one of their own has taken the Second Breath, that one is quickly sent into exile. The child is fostered with a relative in a far-away village not yet under the Bull\u2019s sway if possible, or sent south to Cherak or some other coastal city. Many never make it to their final destination, as travel in the North is dangerous even for armed bands, let alone an untrained child traveling alone or with strangers. Those who do make it to the southern colonies are welcomed with offers of training and education, as few in those hard cities can afford to do without every asset they can acquire.</div> </div> </div> </div>How many newly exalted Dragon-Blooded are these patrols encountering that words like &quot;many&quot; are being invoked?<br /> <br /> It feels like this could be a compelling backstory for a northern Outcaste trying to muster support to fight the Icewalkers but talking about it in such general terms looks like a refugee crisis and gives the Bull a very hard-line stance on Dragon-Blooded that could have a significant impact on how PCs perceive him and his goals that's news to the person who wrote his section in Compass North.<br /> <br /> The Outcaste demographics often paint very different pictures of societies to other sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-05-2017, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T18:48:02-08:00","id":1058730,"title":"","content":"This thread made me take another hard look at the map, as I too was originally perplexed by some of the flourishes, and I noticed something.<br /> <br /> Some of the circled areas have a little line coming off of them with some small text, which I believe is supposed to represent that they are magnified, and by how much, but only with in-setting squiggles.<br /> <br /> The other circles seem to represent either emphasis, or sphere of influence. The Scavenger Lands has a circle, there's a sublte one around the Blessed Isle and Threshold, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T02:41:44-08:00","id":1058841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058364#post1058364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels like this could be a compelling backstory for a northern Outcaste trying to muster support to fight the Icewalkers but talking about it in such general terms looks like a refugee crisis and gives the Bull a very hard-line stance on Dragon-Blooded that could have a significant impact on how PCs perceive him and his goals that's news to the person who wrote his section in Compass North.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's important to remember that he's not just a narrative figure but someone the PCs are going to interact with and someone wanting to turn the tables on the Dragon-Blooded and make them the hunted ones isn't just a failure to turn the other cheek and be a bigger person but the nature of Terrestrial Exaltation gives it this added element of ethnic cleansing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058300#post1058300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh not really hunting down and murdering children then. I mean still not exactly a good thing, but from how Lioness phrased it I thought it was something like &quot;That one flared. Slaughter their family, every DB in the north dies.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It might not be much better. The way the villagers are approaching this problem suggests they are much more scared of what the Bull of the North might do if his patrols find a Dragon-Blooded than they are concerned for the individual in question's safety unless all notion of common sense has gone out the window.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T03:33:03-08:00","id":1058860,"title":"","content":"Do not forget the prefacing paragraph. It is not just Icewalker tribes under the influence of Yurgen.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dragonblooded</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Terrestrial children of the icewalker tribes face a difficult choice, and one not their own. Their fate is left in the hands of the animal master that watches over their tribe. They may stay if the animal master allows, and those who do stay tend to become great hunters, champions or even leaders of their tribes. If the animal master exiles them from the tribe, the young Dragon-Blooded must flee, often with little more than the clothing on their backs, or face their own families and friends in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note: Animal Masters are totemic gods of mammoth, reindeer, whales, penguins, and other beasts of importance to life in the North that have cults of devotees among the Icewalker tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T03:48:47-08:00","id":1058865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058730#post1058730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the circled areas have a little line coming off of them with some small text, which I believe is supposed to represent that they are magnified, and by how much, but only with in-setting squiggles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that one of those surrounds the Skullstone Archipelago, and it has two lines leading to dots coming off of it. Also most of the others only surrounds the city icon, so what exactly is being magnified?<br /> <br /> \u200bI've come to suspect that they are <i>all </i>sphere of influence markers, some with in-setting warning notes attached.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T00:51:31-08:00","id":1059379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1052247-ysyr-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=1058860#post1058860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do not forget the prefacing paragraph. It is not just Icewalker tribes under the influence of Yurgen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not forgetting it but the people in the villages aren't Icewalkers and the Animal Masters with a policy of exiling Dragon-Blooded from their tribes aren't highly successful expansionist warlords that my PC might feel a sense of comradery to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}